{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced","id":1531801,"title":"Werewolf the Apocalypse 5th - Shattered Nation Announced","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-01T13:30:13-08:00","id":1531801,"title":"Werewolf the Apocalypse 5th - Shattered Nation Announced","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced#post1531801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Society of the Garou Unveiled</i><br /> <br /> Once the Garou tribes were united in one mighty Nation, ready and willing to fight for Gaia whenever and wherever they needed to. Now as the Apocalypse rages, the mightiest bulwark that should have defended against it is in tatters. The Garou Nation lies shattered.<br /> <br /> <i>Shattered Nation </i>is a setting book for Werewolf, detailing the ruins of the Garou Nation and how they can be used concretely in <b>Werewolf </b>stories but it also details opportunities the players\u2019 pack has in Garou politics, to leverage their Renown for power and influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Features</b><ul><li>Explore pack dynamics (including new Pack types)</li> <li>Take action as a pack</li> <li>Use, Learn, and Portray the Rites of the Garou, including new Rites</li> <li>Run and participate in Moots</li> <li>Deal with the enemies</li> <li>Add 7 new loresheets to their characters</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>it's Renegade game studios book,i feel like it might solve some issues most of us have with w5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T14:09:14-08:00","id":1531804,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing much to get my hopes up in that regard.<br /> <br /> - The blurb focuses on the Nation already being broken, not on any discussions of how that happened (esp. as something that's supposed to have been a fairly recent event but with excruciatingly little acknowledgement of). The phrasing of, &quot;detailing the ruins of the Garou Nation and how they can be used concretely&quot; feels like it's just going to be more of the same, &quot;if you want actual lore and world building, W5 isn't the game for you,&quot; than a fix to how little the impact of the shattering of the Nation is really established.<br /> <br /> - More stuff on packs is good. Not sure that addresses many of the big complaints about the game as it currently stands.<br /> <br /> - More Rites doesn't fix the problems with the mechanical implementation of Rites. Unless there's going to be some seriously major &quot;optional&quot; rules here to make Rites something people want to use more, it's largely wasted space. Even if it tries to reestablish the former place Rites had as central parts of Garou social interactions, the mechanics will get in the way of them filling that role.<br /> <br /> - Again, unless there's a huge improvement via &quot;optional&quot; rules, Moots don't work in the RAW, so having a section on them is, at best, some cool fluff that will be out of step with the RAW.<br /> <br /> - &quot;Deal with enemies&quot; is far to vague to preview anything meaningful about the text.<br /> <br /> - More loresheets is fine. The core book certainly could have used more if Loresheets are going to be as important to W5 as they are for V5. But this isn't a major concern in and of itself. Given that some of the core Loresheets are things people have active complaints about, more of them could add in more questionable things like being able to redeem BSDs. So this isn't reassuring to the bigger picture of the issues with the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T14:19:19-08:00","id":1531805,"title":"","content":"Looking at this feature list, it's not really approaching the iceberg of concerns. Also, it's slightly concerning that all they feel they have to show for the Nation are Rites and Moots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T14:26:01-08:00","id":1531807,"title":"","content":"i mean, previous editions had dozens of books to build a setting, this one is still at its beginning. it stands to reason that when w5 has a ton of books to its name it's setting will be pretty expansive too.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531805#post1531805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at this feature list, it's not really approaching the iceberg of concerns. Also, it's slightly concerning that all they feel they have to show for the Nation are Rites and Moots?</div> </div> </div> </div>one thing that w5 likes to do in it's portrayal of the garou is that the w5 garou,they don't have like.... an overachieving mission,y'know? they don't have a larger calling,a bigger mission or acoordinated goal. in previous editions the garou had a very clearly defined list of do's and don't's,they had a list of tasks they were bound to perform,they had obligations, rn they can choose their own path, they can do whatever they want.<br /> so within werewolf5 designs goals it makes sense that the Nation,as it stands,is much looser because the garou's mission,or lack of it, is much looser","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 03-01-2024, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T14:59:02-08:00","id":1531812,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Once the Garou tribes were united in one mighty Nation, ready and willing to fight for Gaia whenever and wherever they needed to. Now as the Apocalypse rages, the mightiest bulwark that should have defended against it is in tatters. The Garou Nation lies shattered.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This is such a weird way to start the blurb. Like, there are the poems on the backcovers of WtA books detailing how these are the last days. But one thing they don't say is that the fight is already lost.<br /> <br /> This outright says &quot;There was a force fighting, once. Now it is lost&quot; and then doesn't follow it up with &quot;But there is still hope, as the younger generation of garou prepare to claim what was lost.&quot; It follows it up with &quot;And here are tools you can use for the Nation in its ruined state.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, I know this sounds like a broken record, but if the Apocalypse IS raging, why doesn't it feel like it is? I don't mean in terms of the garou, I mean in terms of the world. The Apocalypse is not the end of the Nation or the garou, the Apocalypse is supposed to be the end of the WORLD.<br /> <br /> So why can you still be a barista? XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T15:05:29-08:00","id":1531813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531812#post1531812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Once the Garou tribes were united in one mighty Nation, ready and willing to fight for Gaia whenever and wherever they needed to. Now as the Apocalypse rages, the mightiest bulwark that should have defended against it is in tatters. The Garou Nation lies shattered.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This is such a weird way to start the blurb. Like, there are the poems on the backcovers of WtA books detailing how these are the last days. But one thing they don't say is that the fight is already lost.<br /> <br /> This outright says &quot;There was a force fighting, once. Now it is lost&quot; and then doesn't follow it up with &quot;But there is still hope, as the younger generation of garou prepare to claim what was lost.&quot; It follows it up with &quot;And here are tools you can use for the Nation in its ruined state.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, I know this sounds like a broken record, but if the Apocalypse IS raging, why doesn't it feel like it is? I don't mean in terms of the garou, I mean in terms of the world. The Apocalypse is not the end of the Nation or the garou, the Apocalypse is supposed to be the end of the WORLD.<br /> <br /> So why can you still be a barista? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>'yknow that's actually a fun thing to talk about.<br /> &quot;Apocalypse&quot; as a <i>word, </i>does <i>not </i>mean &quot;the end of the world&quot; it doesn't means &quot;everyone will have terrible time&quot;,it doesn't mean &quot;we're all screwed&quot;<br /> &quot;Apocalypse&quot; just means &quot;Revelation&quot;,as in &quot;a old truth,once hidden is now revealed&quot;.<br /> that's definitely interesting to think about in the context of the wod","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T15:17:35-08:00","id":1531814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531807#post1531807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i mean, previous editions had dozens of books to build a setting, this one is still at its beginning. it stands to reason that when w5 has a ton of books to its name it's setting will be pretty expansive too.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you really want to stack up W1 vs W5 in terms of how much world building got done, we can, but I'm not sure you're going to get the results you're hoping for.<br /> <br /> While Paradox said it, not Renegade, W5 was designed to eschew the lore and world building that permeated the previous editions. W5 isn't so lacking because it's just one book. It's lacking because it was purposefully made that way; beyond the whole &quot;re imagining&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to assume the Renegade is going to buck Paradox's initial design approach and start world building like mad to try to get W5 to where the game used to be in terms of setting depth. A dozen more books can easily keep up the whole, &quot;Maybe it happened this way, maybe that way, who knows? We're not going to tell you even if it seems like it would be really important to know the answer.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> one thing that w5 likes to do in it's portrayal of the garou is that the w5 garou,they don't have like.... an overachieving mission,y'know? they don't have a larger calling,a bigger mission or acoordinated goal. </div> </div> </div>W5 didn't dump the idea that the Garou have an overarching mission. It just had them fail. The calling is still present, but so fair they're aimless in how to do anything about it. This book could actually address this a bit, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in previous editions the garou had a very clearly defined list of do's and don't's,they had a list of tasks they were bound to perform,they had obligations, rn they can choose their own path, they can do whatever they want. </div> </div> </div>The Litany still exists in W5. Renown still exists to enforce those social norms and standards. The consequences for going off and doing your own thing are different, not the capability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so within werewolf5 designs goals it makes sense that the Nation,as it stands,is much looser because the garou's mission,or lack of it, is much looser </div> </div> </div>This really doesn't hold up to scrutiny. The Nation isn't &quot;looser&quot; it's broken. It's in &quot;ruins.&quot; It's &quot;shattered.&quot; The mission hasn't changed, the situation has changed. Not knowing how to do your calling isn't the same as having a looser set of mission parameters. There's just nobody in a position to seriously punish you for going off mission.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531813#post1531813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'yknow that's actually a fun thing to talk about</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> that's definitely interesting to think about in the context of the wod </div> </div> </div>To me it just sounds like equivocation. We know that in WtA &quot;apocalypse&quot; has the newer meaning of &quot;end times&quot; derived from the Book of Revelations as it described the end times. It's not some deep word play.<br /> <br /> &quot;Armageddon&quot; was originally just a place name. So was &quot;Gehenna.&quot; But these things take on additional meanings and contexts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 03-01-2024, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T15:26:22-08:00","id":1531816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531813#post1531813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'yknow that's actually a fun thing to talk about.<br /> &quot;Apocalypse&quot; as a <i>word, </i>does <i>not </i>mean &quot;the end of the world&quot; it doesn't means &quot;everyone will have terrible time&quot;,it doesn't mean &quot;we're all screwed&quot;<br /> &quot;Apocalypse&quot; just means &quot;Revelation&quot;,as in &quot;a old truth,once hidden is now revealed&quot;.<br /> that's definitely interesting to think about in the context of the wod</div> </div> </div> </div>Etymology is all well and good, but we aren't talking about what the word means in general.<br /> <br /> In WtA lore, the A in the abbreviation has always been indicating how important the concept of an apocalypse IS to the game. In WtA lore, the apocalypse IS the end of everything. That is what the garou were trying to prevent, hence why the modern game has always been set during the last days BEFORE the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> This is akin to if V5 did away with the Masquerade but still had the word in the title.<br /> <br /> W5, despite still having Apocalypse in the title, isn't about the apocalypse. The apocalypse is an background event to the focus which is garou eking out territories and fighting one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T15:34:13-08:00","id":1531817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531813#post1531813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'yknow that's actually a fun thing to talk about.<br /> &quot;Apocalypse&quot; as a <i>word, </i>does <i>not </i>mean &quot;the end of the world&quot; it doesn't means &quot;everyone will have terrible time&quot;,it doesn't mean &quot;we're all screwed&quot;<br /> &quot;Apocalypse&quot; just means &quot;Revelation&quot;,as in &quot;a old truth,once hidden is now revealed&quot;.<br /> that's definitely interesting to think about in the context of the wod</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the revelation, it could be anything, like that the veil has fallen, that the supernatural including werewolves and formori have now been revealed to humans (in which case the government would hide it from the general public) or maybe they want to reveal a horrible truth about the werewolves, like they are a corruption of the Wyrm or that they are just a curse having nothing to do with the triad and Gaia, then they can go down different paths, like the Garou having to live as a cursed existence, or them believing that the apocalypse It is their trial of redemption. Okay, maybe it's not bad ideia, but I'm in disbelief or just a history about survivor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T15:43:03-08:00","id":1531818,"title":"","content":"Okay, what I would really like to know how the tribes and Garou organized themselves at the time of the apocalypse. In the revised editions the tribes themselves had different caerns and groups with varying approaches, it would be good to have examples of how each tribe and group acted to survive the apocalypse and deal with hunters, including neutral groups, this would give insight into what is happening and give examples of interesting chronicles with the theme of survival. I'm not saying that this would fix anything, but I would find it particularly interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:18:34-08:00","id":1531822,"title":"","content":"so,don't quote me on this,because i very well might be wrong but after watching the announcement stream it seems like part of the book is about a player character pack actually rebuilding the garou nation.<br /> edit: by receiving Jonas' crown","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 03-01-2024, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:41:17-08:00","id":1531824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/live/SkAA2LBB8dw?si=G74VwG24wFD4aEBA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/live/SkAA2LBB8dw?si=G74VwG24wFD4aEBA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/live/SkAA2LBB8dw?si=G74VwG24wFD4aEBA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/live/SkAA2LBB8dw?si=G74VwG24wFD4aEBA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;He's the last king of the Silver Fang and by extension the Garou Nation as a whole but as the tribes fractured, albrecht finds himself as kings of this shattered nation, a relic of the past where the unity of the tribes still meant something,he's got a crown there which was once a symbol of the unity of the nation,but the nation has cracked and fallen the crown is not in great in shape. basically he was a great hero once upon a time in a past generation,someone gotta bring the nation back together.someone younger,maybe someone in your pack?&quot;<br /> Kevin from renegade game studios","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 03-01-2024, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:53:38-08:00","id":1531826,"title":"","content":"I will say this for W5 its mentioned The Silver Crown more times than any of the WtA Chronicles I've run, played in or read over the last three decades ever did....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T18:45:14-08:00","id":1531832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531824#post1531824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/live/SkAA2LBB8dw?si=G74VwG24wFD4aEBA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/live/SkAA2LB...4VwG24wFD4aEBA</a><br /> <br /> &quot;He's the last king of the Silver Fang and by extension the Garou Nation as a whole but as the tribes fractured, albrecht finds himself as kings of this shattered nation, a relic of the past where the unity of the tribes still meant something,he's got a crown there which was once a symbol of the unity of the nation,but the nation has cracked and fallen the crown is not in great in shape. basically he was a great hero once upon a time in a past generation,someone gotta bring the nation back together.someone younger,maybe someone in your pack?&quot;<br /> Kevin from renegade game studios</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they going to go into how if the Silver Crown doesn't like you it'll burn right through your head and kill you?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm leery of books that push pack organization in W5, because I suspect that it'll just be a truncated, ill-fitting version of Forsaken when it isn't just copying how coteries work and what they do from Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T19:54:38-08:00","id":1531835,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts:<ul><li>Covering what the setting with the fallen Garou Nation looks like is a good addition but this should've been covered by the corebook already. I wonder how in-depth they actually can be or will even try considering the page-count-limitations of this supplement.</li> <li>Pack types are another good addition - which also should've been covered by the corebook already. That way a supplement like this would've had the room to introduce an expanded Pack-type-creation a la the V5 Players Guide.</li> <li>&quot;Taking action as a pack&quot; sounds to me like it will be another one of those &quot;Use a relationship-map to depict conflicts and handle Project rules&quot;. Again, something that should've been covered by the corebook because Blood Sigils for example builds on that by delving into a specific variant of using those rules for blood sorcery. Instead, the supplement will have to cover the basics here, I imagine.</li> <li>For the Rites, Kevin mentioned during the stream that there will be like 12 Rites and most of them will be of a mystical variety and they correspond to Auspices (but they're also so broad that everybody can use them). Don't think more Rites is exactly what this game needed but I'm also surprised the book didn't go for listing new Gifts instead.</li> <li>7 new Loresheets. Ah, good, the numbers are rising (Blood Sigils had 4 Loresheets, for example).</li> <li>The Silver Crown bit from the stream sounds like one of the Loresheets will be &quot;Albrecht's newest BFF&quot; or something like that. From Kevin's description in the W5 timeline Jonas Albrecht was the last King of the Garou with the Silver Crown. That has all sorts of implications about the setting (for one thing it means the Fall of the Garou Nation happened in living memory). Hmm, I guess we're gonna see if they make this work.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T22:40:08-08:00","id":1531836,"title":"","content":"I have to be honest, W5 would do so much better if it tried to do its own thing and not bring old stuff back. Because things like the Last Gaian King have so much in-universe build up that bringing Alby to W5 makes very little sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T00:21:48-08:00","id":1531837,"title":"","content":"As said the majority of this sounds like ' stuff that should have been in the corebook' but as its a Renegade book and not inhouse I wonder if it will vary from Corebook W5 as much as the free Renegade books and adventure scenarios have so far? I mean the Core is extremely vague about what the Nation was even like yet Shattered Nation and Albrecht being alive/recently dead means that its really, really recent that the Nation crumbled into nothing so we still have the issue of why no one remembers anything........unless thats going to be 'retconned' and this book will fill in all the society and culture gaps that are missing from the Core which, yes seems a little cash-grabby but eh thats standard Paradox at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T07:27:00-08:00","id":1531881,"title":"","content":"I don't think the &quot;broken Garou Nation&quot; is anything new. I think it just reflects the Stargazers left and the Get of Fenris became evil.<br /> <br /> Which, fair, 2 tribes leaving in twenty years with one in active revolt is definitely enough to make that accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T09:24:06-08:00","id":1531892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531881#post1531881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the &quot;broken Garou Nation&quot; is anything new. I think it just reflects the Stargazers left and the Get of Fenris became evil.<br /> <br /> Which, fair, 2 tribes leaving in twenty years with one in active revolt is definitely enough to make that accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it seems from the info we have on SN ( from the press release and statements made by Renegade.) that The Nation was intact during JAs rulership, assuming ( and its a fair assumption) he took up the crown in his mid 40s like in Legacy then him being in his 60s-70s ( judging from the art ) means it all happened in the last couple of decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T10:35:32-08:00","id":1531902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531892#post1531892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it seems from the info we have on SN ( from the press release and statements made by Renegade.) that The Nation was intact during JAs rulership, assuming ( and its a fair assumption) he took up the crown in his mid 40s like in Legacy then him being in his 60s-70s ( judging from the art ) means it all happened in the last couple of decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <i>The Postman</i> level of memory degradation, there. Maybe even worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T11:10:14-08:00","id":1531905,"title":"","content":"The big change that W5 has introduced is that the Garou-Nation isn't just in a crisis or broken, it's fallen, sundered, it's <i>just gone</i>. The Garou-Nation is a thing of the past in the W5-setting. After all, that's how we got this colorful line from the W5 corebook (pg 47): &quot;For all of the self-glorifying tales that old Garou tell around the fires, younger werewolves note that the Garou Nation didn\u2019t collapse because the Litany was so goddamn perfect.&quot; But the W5 corebook never explains when that happened, how that happened exactly and how things have changed for Garou between the time there was a Garou-Nation and the time when this societal structure collapsed and disappeared. And what these previews suggest is that Albrecht is part of this new W5 canon, that he was the last King of the Garou-Nation before it fell and that he (with his Silver Crown) is still around (which means the fall of the Garou Nation happened quite recently).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T11:17:51-08:00","id":1531907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531905#post1531905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And what these previews suggest is that Albrecht is part of this new W5 canon, that he was the last King of the Garou-Nation before it fell and that he (with his Silver Crown) is still around (which means the fall of the Garou Nation happened quite recently).</div> </div> </div> </div>It also raises another two questions; Why is it gone and how is it gone?<br /> <br /> The Nation is very loosely organized, with septs mostly doing their own thing. Even a major sept like Shigalu falling didn't break the Nation, so what did?<br /> <br /> As well, how does this fall LOOK in practise? You can still have multi-tribal packs, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T11:52:09-08:00","id":1531910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531907#post1531907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also raises another two questions; Why is it gone and how is it gone?<br /> <br /> The Nation is very loosely organized, with septs mostly doing their own thing. Even a major sept like Shigalu falling didn't break the Nation, so what did?<br /> <br /> As well, how does this fall LOOK in practise? You can still have multi-tribal packs, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, worldbuilding (or more like the lack thereof) is a general problem of the W5 corebook. It's necessary to address questions like that to understand the W5 setting, so it's good that this supplement is covering that but really, this should've been covered already in the W5 corebook. The story of Albrecht, the last king of the Garou Nation, as a character would've been a good focus to tell the story of how the fall of the Garou Nation happened.<br /> <br /> On one hand, I can't picture a Renegade-supplement really delving into any sort of deep backstory with this supplement (as other Renegade supplement haven't really done anything like that) but on the other hand previously with the V5 supplements you could rely on other books having covered the basics of who did what. When the writers for Blood Sigils wrote about the Vienna incident, they had more information than &quot;The Tremere chantry in Vienna is destroyed - but we don't know who did it and how and when that happened.&quot;. Therefore, that book could comfortably delve into the aftereffects of that incident. But writing about the fallen Garou-Nation presents you with a serious lack of information when it comes to the W5 corebook. There's no depth to explore here because you first have to establish what's even going on in this case.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T12:29:15-08:00","id":1531913,"title":"","content":"I feel the wrong lessons are learned here. What we were protesting was a lack of world building and an incredibly heavy handed approach to anything that was core to the old experience of Werewolf. Renegade/Paradox feels that the solution to this is to bring back metaplot and events leading to the Silver Crown being handed from Albrecht to the PC's.<br /> <br /> What the ever loving fuck?<br /> <br /> Albrecht's best trait was that he was an absent king. He was focused on being a hero that inspires and a questing king rather than the big organiser who would make things work in a specific way. Konietzko was the one that fulfilled the second role. And both of them were figures that were not monolithic and that would not impact or impair any games that didn't need them.<br /> <br /> Now their solution is to bring back the last king and have him hand over his duty to the PC's for... what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T12:42:02-08:00","id":1531915,"title":"","content":"I can't say there is anything wrong with the book's premise, much au contraire, but it is undeniable that Moots, pack actions and more setting stuff should've been in the corebook already. No doubt!<br /> <br /> The rest we will have to watch and see. While I have problems with the producers and directors of W5 (not the writers and designers), the game and system itself, and the themes of the game are generally in a very good spot for me (that never liked Werewolf that much, and particularly thought that the 20th anniversary editions were good, not the greatest thing ever made). So I'm curious to see what the first true supplement book of W5 gives us, if its cool and juicy or dry and whack. <br /> <br /> Like many WoD games, the society of the denizens of Darkness is a very important part of the game, and that was sorely missing from the corebook. I don't find the whole Garou nation that interesting as a whole, a bit too universalist for me. But hell, for sure the packs would have whole communities in their regions, and Tribes would work more broadly (just not in every continent). Having a book about these societies was very much needed indeed.<br /> <br /> I don't think - like pretty much every single future releasing book would - this book will change the opinion of anyone who already dislikes W5. Which is a shame. But, we will have to way and see if it does give good material for the game at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T12:46:33-08:00","id":1531916,"title":"","content":"Also, so, okay, you bring back Albrecht as the old and broken king so that he can hand over the reins to a new generation of young Garou (presumably the PCs). And the generational conflict between older and younger Garou is an established thing in W5. But then the whole thing crashes immediately into another big issue of W5. Okay, so Albrecht thinks these young Garou are really cool, he gives them (or one of them) the Silver Crown... and now what? We hit upon another big issue of the W5 corebook: What exactly are Garou supposed to do in W5? (... other than realize that Garou are the wrong tool to solve the world's problems, of course) I mean, why even rebuild the Garou Nation when you have sentiments like &quot;The Litany sucks.&quot; mentioned in the W5 corebook. Not only is there a sentiment that the old guard failed but that it failed because it was bad. The young Garou aren't described as saying stuff like &quot;Oh man, I wish, we could bring back the Garou Nation.&quot;. And that then taps into yet another issue where it isn't clear what the new thing they want to pursue instead is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T12:48:15-08:00","id":1531917,"title":"","content":"I may be wrong but I feel the shards of Hope such as the Ahadi, Bats Redemption and other steps towards reform/amends were the most used parts of the, fairly scant, metaplot of WtA. The Last King, Perfect Metis and Anthelios only appeared in very specific kinds of Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T12:56:52-08:00","id":1531919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531917#post1531917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be wrong but I feel the shards of Hope such as the Ahadi, Bats Redemption and other steps towards reform/amends were the most used parts of the, fairly scant, metaplot of WtA. The Last King, Perfect Metis and Anthelios only appeared in very specific kinds of Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>When people discuss metaplot they usually talk about Vampire, Mage Reviseed and the Time of Judgement. What people tend to miss is the simple fact that the metaplot of Werewolf was incredibly open towards player engagement and about building up a bigger world with more ideas, rather than defining a one true way how everything is going to fall apart. It was about Creation and Change rather then about spiraling into selfdestruction and crying in the ashes of what could have been.<br /> <br /> Ironic for a game that's all about the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T12:58:40-08:00","id":1531920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531915#post1531915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...that never liked Werewolf that much...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you're happy with your purchase and found a game you enjoy. However, there is a very clear strain in the community between people who disliked what Werewolf used to be and are happy with what was served up as W5, and the rest of us who feel that it gutted the soul of the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T13:22:14-08:00","id":1531922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531915#post1531915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I have problems with the producers and directors of W5 (not the writers and designers), the game and system itself, and the themes of the game are generally in a very good spot for me (that never liked Werewolf that much, and particularly thought that the 20th anniversary editions were good, not the greatest thing ever made).</div> </div> </div> </div>My dread for this book is that it won't play into those things that made W5 stand out (as flawed as they are), but a return to the older way of WtA.<br /> <br /> W5 has the tools to play a more 'typical' werewolf game, something it should embrace rather than try to bring back the old canon.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T15:14:28-08:00","id":1531926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531913#post1531913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the wrong lessons are learned here. What we were protesting was a lack of world building and an incredibly heavy handed approach to anything that was core to the old experience of Werewolf. Renegade/Paradox feels that the solution to this is to bring back metaplot and events leading to the Silver Crown being handed from Albrecht to the PC's.<br /> <br /> What the ever loving fuck?<br /> <br /> Albrecht's best trait was that he was an absent king. He was focused on being a hero that inspires and a questing king rather than the big organiser who would make things work in a specific way. Konietzko was the one that fulfilled the second role. And both of them were figures that were not monolithic and that would not impact or impair any games that didn't need them.<br /> <br /> Now their solution is to bring back the last king and have him hand over his duty to the PC's for... what?</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious thing would be for PCs to be a force for change. I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T15:26:01-08:00","id":1531927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531926#post1531926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The obvious thing would be for PCs to be a force for change. I imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking about the same game that specifically says the Garou are not able to change anything due to their nature? Or the same game that tells us that the Garou have lost and that there is nothing left to fight for but your own turf? Where the developers have specifically told us we're not supposed to change the world but be happy that we kept a small bit of it alive just a bit longer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T15:32:37-08:00","id":1531929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531892#post1531892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it seems from the info we have on SN ( from the press release and statements made by Renegade.) that The Nation was intact during JAs rulership, assuming ( and its a fair assumption) he took up the crown in his mid 40s like in Legacy then him being in his 60s-70s ( judging from the art ) means it all happened in the last couple of decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, my point is that the Garou Nation breaking is a recent thing. The Cult of Fenris only left in the Time of Judgement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T16:19:30-08:00","id":1531930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531927#post1531927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are we talking about the same game that specifically says the Garou are not able to change anything due to their nature? Or the same game that tells us that the Garou have lost and that there is nothing left to fight for but your own turf? Where the developers have specifically told us we're not supposed to change the world but be happy that we kept a small bit of it alive just a bit longer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, the crown can still be used symbolically so it can be useful to unite groups that still believe in some unity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T18:10:48-08:00","id":1531939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531922#post1531922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My dread for this book is that it won't play into those things that made W5 stand out (as flawed as they are), but a return to the older way of WtA.<br /> <br /> W5 has the tools to play a more 'typical' werewolf game, something it should embrace rather than try to bring back the old canon.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If people want that they could have gone with pretty much any other game. In fact, one wonders why Paradox didn't just make their own IP; not much about V:tM really stands out from other vampire media, and if they're trying for broad-net, ripped from the Universal movies play, the rest of the WoD is pretty much an impediment to that. We've already seen that V:tM has also suffered a hard fall from the days of trying to move in on D&amp;D's numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T02:40:52-08:00","id":1531946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531922#post1531922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My dread for this book is that it won't play into those things that made W5 stand out (as flawed as they are), but a return to the older way of WtA.<br /> <br /> W5 has the tools to play a more 'typical' werewolf game, something it should embrace rather than try to bring back the old canon.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically it would repeat the pattern of how many people online have handled the lack of lore/worldbuilding in W5. So why wouldn't the same thing come true for the Renegade writers? You're an ST and you want to have a Moot in your game, the W5 corebook doesn't offer much and so what do you do...? You just go back to the books from previous editions and look at what they say about Moots. Similarly, you're tasked as a writer to write about Moots for this supplement. Do you just invent something completely new or... do you simply go back to the old books and copy established lore from there? And why wouldn't you do the latter? Moot was brought over from previous editions, to begin with. If it were really supposed to be so different, why didn't the W5 corebook writers come up with something new and original from the very beginning? So it wouldn't surprise me if it becomes a pattern for these W5 supplements to liberally borrow/copy stuff from previous editions and bring that stuff back into W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T05:31:05-08:00","id":1531950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531946#post1531946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it wouldn't surprise me if it becomes a pattern for these W5 supplements to liberally borrow/copy stuff from previous editions and bring that stuff back into W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how much that goes against the spirit of the corebook, but you are right that it doesn't offer much to actually do.<br /> <br /> It is just really bad planning to have a book decry the old ways and then later go &quot;wait no, they weren't that bad!&quot;<br /> <br /> So we end up with the situation that Changeling the Dreaming was in for ages, where the core was a incoherent mess and it was the additional books that brought the value to the game XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T06:06:09-08:00","id":1531951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531950#post1531950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder how much that goes against the spirit of the corebook, but you are right that it doesn't offer much to actually do.<br /> <br /> It is just really bad planning to have a book decry the old ways and then later go &quot;wait no, they weren't that bad!&quot;<br /> <br /> So we end up with the situation that Changeling the Dreaming was in for ages, where the core was a incoherent mess and it was the additional books that brought the value to the game XD</div> </div> </div> </div>It already kinda goes against the corebook by simply bringing back Albrecht, the last king of the Garou, as a character because there's a sidebar for the Silver Crown on pg 190 and this is what it says: &quot;As a symbol of its grandeur, the Silver Fangs tribe exalts the Silver Crown, a legendary artifact belonging to the Albrecht lineage of Silver Fang werewolves. With the disappearance of the last proclaimed king of the tribe, however, two great icons of tribal esteem have been lost, which many Garou interpret as an omen about the fate of the Silver Fangs.&quot; If Albrecht as a character comes back, this reference to an &quot;Albrecht lineage&quot; sounds weird. (Also reminds me that the fall of the Garou Nation should've had a way bigger impact on how the Silver Fangs are presented in the book but that's a whole other thing...)<br /> <br /> But I think that passage is a good example of how the W5 corebook writing gets itself trapped between a rock and a hard place for no reason. If you don't want any of the metaplot from previous editions, all you need is to say that Silver Fangs were traditionally picked as kings of the Garou Nation. When the Nation fell, the Silver Crown disappeared. Done. There's no need to mention Albrecht at all. And yet, they take this strange step of mentioning Albrecht but then also want to make clear it is not a continuation of previous editions, so now it's instead the &quot;Albrecht lineage&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:32:50-08:00","id":1531962,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll be interested in seeing where they go with this book, if only because it strongly suggests that WEREWOLF 5th Edition is, in many ways, a post-Apocalyptic setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:45:16-08:00","id":1531966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531962#post1531962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I\u2019ll be interested in seeing where they go with this book, if only because it strongly suggests that WEREWOLF 5th Edition is, in many ways, a post-Apocalyptic setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that within the WtA-setting, a post-apocalypse-setting can't exist. The titular &quot;Apocalypse&quot; in WtA (and in this case I'm quoting the W5 corebook specifically) is defined as: &quot;The physical and spiritual end of the world, brought about by relentless human greed and consumption&quot; The &quot;Apocalypse&quot; in WtA is the literal end of everything in existence.<br /> <br /> Now what could be an interesting move, I think, would be to use post-Apocalypse-tropes to describe the fallen Garou-Nation but not have the setting/world as such be post-apocalyptic. Stuff like focusing on survival, scarcity of resources (like caerns, for example) and a dog-eat-dog-attitude between Garou-Septs. I think that could work. But it would require this supplement to do some heavy lifting to make the worldbuilding work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:47:45-08:00","id":1531967,"title":"","content":"Now that you mention it, \u201cA post-Apocalyptic organisation in an Apocalyptic setting\u201d <i>would</i> be a more elegant statement of the High Concept that occurred to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T16:09:33-08:00","id":1531982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531950#post1531950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So we end up with the situation that <b>Kindred of the East </b>was in for ages, where the core was a incoherent mess and it was the additional books that brought the value to the game XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Also WtF 1st, MtAw 1st....and many others.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T04:57:57-08:00","id":1532002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531929#post1531929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, my point is that the Garou Nation breaking is a recent thing. The Cult of Fenris only left in the Time of Judgement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Word of Line Developer is that there never was a Time of Judgement in W5. W5 is a reboot and there never was a set of events that led from Legacy into the world of W5. No matter how much you (or I) want it to be otherwise, you are going against what the author and the book tell us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T05:00:12-08:00","id":1532003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531982#post1531982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also WtF 1st, MtAw 1st....and many others.....</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE got so much better with the suppements. The core's attitude, sinocentrism and Kill Whitey crap was quickly developed away into something that is more inlusive of the vast diversity that is the Asian continent. Have you seen HsienFan's amazing new version of KotE, btw?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T05:21:54-08:00","id":1532005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532002#post1532002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Word of Line Developer is that there never was a Time of Judgement in W5. W5 is a reboot and there never was a set of events that led from Legacy into the world of W5. No matter how much you (or I) want it to be otherwise, you are going against what the author and the book tell us.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're saying in universe when I'm talking Out of Universe. The Get of Fenris falling is something based on what we had in previous canon.<br /> <br /> Also, it's a &quot;Re-Imagining&quot; which isn't a reboot.<br /> <br /> They've already started mentioning plenty of WTA stuff in the upcoming supplements. It's just that there's never been Crinosborn or other elements that have been removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T05:53:04-08:00","id":1532006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532005#post1532005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're saying in universe when I'm talking Out of Universe. The Get of Fenris falling is something based on what we had in previous canon.<br /> <br /> Also, it's a &quot;Re-Imagining&quot; which isn't a reboot.<br /> <br /> They've already started mentioning plenty of WTA stuff in the upcoming supplements. It's just that there's never been Crinosborn or other elements that have been removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reboot is a fitting description of what W5 is doing. Previous continuity was discarded and elements from the previous continuity are either being recreated or changed while trying to maintain core-elements of the previous iteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T05:56:49-08:00","id":1532007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532003#post1532003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> KotE got so much better with the suppements. The core's attitude, sinocentrism and Kill Whitey crap was quickly developed away into something that is more inlusive of the vast diversity that is the Asian continent. Have you seen HsienFan's amazing new version of KotE, btw?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its awesome and his rework of C20/Hsien is great too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:49:20-08:00","id":1532018,"title":"","content":"Making lemonade out of lemons is a time-honoured custom of Shared Universe fiction and that ability to do so is as invaluable as chocolate.<br /> <br /> Gold? Diamonds, you say? Well I can live happily enough without either, but try going more than a day without chocolate and see how sufferable the world looks!<br /> <br /> At this point it\u2019s customary to add \u201cI\u2019m not an addict, I can stop any time I want\u201d but this would, in fact, be a truly absurd lie: why would I WANT to stop eating the single most powerful proof that, despite our own sweet selves, God loves us and wants us to be happy?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T15:37:26-08:00","id":1532064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532006#post1532006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reboot is a fitting description of what W5 is doing. Previous continuity was discarded and elements from the previous continuity are either being recreated or changed while trying to maintain core-elements of the previous iteration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know seems they going to take the game line in a more Rise of skywalker style direction if the whole &quot;somehow Albrecht is canon again&quot; thing is any indication...<br /> <br /> I don't know about you guys but backtracking on controversial story decisions dosent say good things about franchise health. Assuming the whole mess isn't caused by miscommunication between underpayed authors...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-05-2024, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T02:26:25-08:00","id":1532073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532064#post1532064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know seems they going to take the game line in a more Rise of skywalker style direction if the whole &quot;somehow Albrecht is canon again&quot; thing is any indication...<br /> <br /> I don't know about you guys but backtracking on controversial story decisions dosent say good things about franchise health. Assuming the whole mess isn't caused by miscommunication between underpayed authors...</div> </div> </div> </div>... And a young Shadow Lord Garou gets introduced and tries to unite a lot of Septs who is at first introduced as an orphan but then turns out to be Konietzko's granddaughter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, the more recreation of old stuff you put into it, the less it is a reboot and more a remake then. But what a mess that would be if the Renegade supplements take all the vagueries and who-knows-shrugging of the W5 corebook and just fill it out with the old canon again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T04:23:06-08:00","id":1532076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532073#post1532073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the more recreation of old stuff you put into it, the less it is a reboot and more a remake then. But what a mess that would be if the Renegade supplements take all the vagueries and who-knows-shrugging of the W5 corebook and just fill it out with the old canon again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that Renegade authors wasn't given much guidance or material for future supplements so they have to mine past lore to keep the content treadmill going,.which is a shame since many recent WTA fan supplements such as werewolf the essentials is doing the same thing <i>and</i> employing the cultural experts parawolf ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T12:08:10-08:00","id":1532094,"title":"","content":"In the spirit of positivity, here are the things I want the book to have;<br /> <br /> -Explanation of WHAT the Apocalypse IS and how it affects the world. No, it can't be climate change, because that has already happened before and the planet was fine afterwards.<br /> <br /> -What does it mean the Nation is shattered, if you can still have multi-tribal packs as the default group of PCs?<br /> <br /> - Explanation on the Litany, how it is followed and how it is not.<br /> <br /> -Either more Patrons OR a Patron creation section.<br /> <br /> -Since there is no Nation, how has the way the garou act changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T12:35:51-08:00","id":1532098,"title":"","content":"I mean the more they canonize the old lore, the better. No one wants a break with the past. We WANT the old stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T13:20:26-08:00","id":1532104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532098#post1532098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the more they canonize the old lore, the better. No one wants a break with the past. We WANT the old stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree with this. Unless they remove quite a few of the features, W5 doesn't really have the mechanics for the old lore.<br /> <br /> To me, the best thing W5 can do is play up to its strengths, which are a more open world with less restrictions and more freedom to be a garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T13:55:26-08:00","id":1532108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532104#post1532104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree with this. Unless they remove quite a few of the features, W5 doesn't really have the mechanics for the old lore.<br /> <br /> To me, the best thing W5 can do is play up to its strengths, which are a more open world with less restrictions and more freedom to be a garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we'll see but basically I see no reason to continue the line with the name W:TA if they're not going to keep the canon.<br /> <br /> Go ahead and retcon chunks if you must but its the characters and events that make the game, not the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:27:27-08:00","id":1532115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532098#post1532098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the more they canonize the old lore, the better. No one wants a break with the past. We WANT the old stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well strictly speaking we already have that via WEREWOLF 20, so it\u2019s perfectly plausible to maintain an Earth-1/Earth-2 situation and merely use a variation on the Old Lore for W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:48:59-08:00","id":1532117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532108#post1532108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we'll see but basically I see no reason to continue the line with the name W:TA if they're not going to keep the canon.<br /> <br /> Go ahead and retcon chunks if you must but its the characters and events that make the game, not the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Atticutus above said, W20 still exists. And W5 was meant to be a Re-Imagening, right? Trying to force the old lore into how W5 works is not going to work, because the old lore has quite a few aspects that the new mechanics make impossible.<br /> <br /> W5 already made a VERY clear difference between it and Legacy, it carries the WtA name more out of branding than actual content. Things like no garou-born, lupus and hispo forms looking like big dogs and there being actual low-content wolfdog garou, rites being dangerous the more garou are around, the way the auspices (don't) work, the way the Patrons work, the cultural amnesia for a culture older than civilization, the way the umbra works,etc.<br /> <br /> This is not WtA legacy, this is an entirely different setting,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T15:40:02-08:00","id":1532121,"title":"","content":"Which isn\u2019t to say that there\u2019s no room at all to borrow notions from the classic editions: I\u2019m only suggesting that they be reinterpreted to fit the W5 paridigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T16:19:53-08:00","id":1532124,"title":"","content":"It's interesting seeing the fault lines developing in places like the official Discord when SN was announced and hinted at bringing Legacy Lore back. The loudest voices singing W5s praises for purging culture, family and tradition and labelling Legacy fans as bigots and right-wingers have been somewhat stymied as other members have embraced bringing back stronger themes and deeper meaning to the setting.....wondering if we'll see a similar break like those in the V5 fandom where many praise OPPs books as the best of V5 and another, much smaller, segment lambasts them as ' not real V5'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T16:25:51-08:00","id":1532125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532115#post1532115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well strictly speaking we already have that via WEREWOLF 20, so it\u2019s perfectly plausible to maintain an Earth-1/Earth-2 situation and merely use a variation on the Old Lore for W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, W20 is awesome and W5 should build off that. They shouldn't be competing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T16:26:58-08:00","id":1532126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532124#post1532124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting seeing the fault lines developing in places like the official Discord when SN was announced and hinted at bringing Legacy Lore back. The loudest voices singing W5s praises for purging culture, family and tradition and labelling Legacy fans as bigots and right-wingers have been somewhat stymied as other members have embraced bringing back stronger themes and deeper meaning to the setting.....wondering if we'll see a similar break like those in the V5 fandom where many praise OPPs books as the best of V5 and another, much smaller, segment lambasts them as ' not real V5'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I kind of find that hilarious. Then again, I have always been a lore junkie and was often the subject of WOD5 fans saying I didn't get it.<br /> <br /> And absolutely, OPP's V5 is the best of the edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-06-2024, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T21:47:10-08:00","id":1532133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532124#post1532124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting seeing the fault lines developing in places like the official Discord when SN was announced and hinted at bringing Legacy Lore back. The loudest voices singing W5s praises for purging culture, family and tradition and labelling Legacy fans as bigots and right-wingers have been somewhat stymied as other members have embraced bringing back stronger themes and deeper meaning to the setting.....wondering if we'll see a similar break like those in the V5 fandom where many praise OPPs books as the best of V5 and another, much smaller, segment lambasts them as ' not real V5'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly with the current state of w5 there's probably a continent of fans who's... open to the idea of the idea of wta supplement written by Flashgitz over anything written by parawolf.<br /> <br /> Not that I whish for Flashgitz to touch anything wod related since whatever they come up with would reach v5 release levels of infamy. Especially if it involves the Black furies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-07-2024, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T22:34:05-08:00","id":1532136,"title":"","content":"Why did you make me google that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T23:46:10-08:00","id":1532137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532124#post1532124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting seeing the fault lines developing in places like the official Discord when SN was announced and hinted at bringing Legacy Lore back. The loudest voices singing W5s praises for purging culture, family and tradition and labelling Legacy fans as bigots and right-wingers have been somewhat stymied as other members have embraced bringing back stronger themes and deeper meaning to the setting.....wondering if we'll see a similar break like those in the V5 fandom where many praise OPPs books as the best of V5 and another, much smaller, segment lambasts them as ' not real V5'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the 'right winger' came from fans being mad at the loss of the Fenrir? XD<br /> <br /> Given what WtA Legacy's content is compared to VtM's, and how much V5 changed versus W5, it'd be interesting to see how big of a divide it will become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T01:23:36-08:00","id":1532139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532137#post1532137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume the 'right winger' came from fans being mad at the loss of the Fenrir? XD<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably originally, its thrown about fairly liberally at all Legacy fans these days. Cos all Garou are really fascist coded dontchaknow so if you played them then so are you.<br /> <br /> As a lot of these folks are active in the V5 section......I'm not really sure what to say.....cos....if playing a Garou makes you fash, what does playing a slaver cannibal rape corpse make you? *shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T01:35:53-08:00","id":1532140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532136#post1532136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you make me google that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oof sorry about that... \ud83d\ude1e<br /> <br /> For what it's worth if Flashgitz ever wrote a supplement it would defently carry a diffrent mood than w5, and hey maybe someone could find it entertaining (?)<br /> <br /> <br /> ...moving on I wonder how w5 sluppment compare to fan projects it would be a interesting none the less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T02:40:26-08:00","id":1532144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532124#post1532124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting seeing the fault lines developing in places like the official Discord when SN was announced and hinted at bringing Legacy Lore back. The loudest voices singing W5s praises for purging culture, family and tradition and labelling Legacy fans as bigots and right-wingers have been somewhat stymied as other members have embraced bringing back stronger themes and deeper meaning to the setting.....wondering if we'll see a similar break like those in the V5 fandom where many praise OPPs books as the best of V5 and another, much smaller, segment lambasts them as ' not real V5'.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I never understood the direction WOD5E took with H5 and W5. Wasn't it enough for there to be divisions in the sense that there are people who prefer 20th Anniversary, CoFD or WOD5E? Now there are two strains of WOD5E as well, there's the V5 lane where with some changes the game overall still tries to be a continuation of the previous editions and the writers try to integrate old lore/worldbuilding into the new version. And then you have H5 and W5 which are outright trying to tell you that they have nothing to do with their previous editions.<br /> <br /> With H5 it's a bit easier to separate it because a lack of understanding of the setting is built into the game, so really the only obvious departure from before is that it's called Hunter the Reckoning but it's not about the Imbued and there are no Imbued to be found in the H5-version (and people consistently keep bringing this up when critiquing H5). And now you had W5 which started with that &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-blurb. It also didn't help that all the vague blank spaces of the W5 corebook wasn't used to say &quot;This is a new version and old lore won't be taken into consideration for future supplements. But the setting is vague enough that if you want to use the old lore instead, you can.&quot;. Instead, the messaging we got was &quot;If you like the old lore, this game isn't for you.&quot;.<br /> <br /> And now it seems like the Renegade-supplements might try to push W5 back into the V5-lane of being somewhat of a continuation. There will be people who similar to the people who think the Onyx Path supplements for V5 aren't &quot;real V5&quot; will consider this direction to also not be &quot;real W5&quot;. Makes you wonder why they changed course. Did the W5 corebook sales disappoint so now Paradox wants to see some course-correction? Or does the Renegade-team just have a different vision for W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T03:20:15-08:00","id":1532145,"title":"","content":"To be a bit optimistic, maybe some of the writers came in saying that they couldn't really figure out how to continue the story? Since the book put a hard limit on what one COULD do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T04:26:54-08:00","id":1532148,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m sure they don\u2019t <i>have</i> to compete, any more than MASQUERADE competes with REQUIEM - it might the coexistence of these two editions is perhaps best regarded as a storytelling opportunity and not any state of hostilities.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I\u2019m quite reasonably certain that W5 makes so much more sense as a setting where the Weaver and not the Wyrm is ascendant that building the setting out from that assumption would solve a great many problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T04:38:59-08:00","id":1532150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532148#post1532148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m sure they don\u2019t <i>have</i> to compete, any more than MASQUERADE competes with REQUIEM - it might the coexistence of these two editions is perhaps best regarded as a storytelling opportunity and not any state of hostilities.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I\u2019m quite reasonably certain that W5 makes so much more sense as a setting where the Weaver and not the Wyrm is ascendant that building the setting out from that assumption would solve a great many problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Try telling that to Paradox... There's a reason you don't see any more new official releases for 20th Anniversary and CofD.<br /> <br /> I agree with you, though. The WOD-brand would've been better served by keeping 20th and CofD and giving themselves room to truly embrace their specific new 5E-take on the WOD. Also, they should've learned from CofD and there should've been a stronger push for H5 and W5 to stay consistent in their similarities with V5 in the same way games in CofD share similarities.<br /> <br /> But alas, here we are instead, with WOD5E possibly going through yet another shift in direction again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T04:47:08-08:00","id":1532153,"title":"","content":"At least it keeps life interesting and gives us an impeccable excuse to argue &amp; grumble!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T06:43:17-08:00","id":1532156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532144#post1532144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I never understood the direction WOD5E took with H5 and W5. Wasn't it enough for there to be divisions in the sense that there are people who prefer 20th Anniversary, CoFD or WOD5E? Now there are two strains of WOD5E as well, there's the V5 lane where with some changes the game overall still tries to be a continuation of the previous editions and the writers try to integrate old lore/worldbuilding into the new version. And then you have H5 and W5 which are outright trying to tell you that they have nothing to do with their previous editions.<br /> <br /> With H5 it's a bit easier to separate it because a lack of understanding of the setting is built into the game, so really the only obvious departure from before is that it's called Hunter the Reckoning but it's not about the Imbued and there are no Imbued to be found in the H5-version (and people consistently keep bringing this up when critiquing H5). And now you had W5 which started with that &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-blurb. It also didn't help that all the vague blank spaces of the W5 corebook wasn't used to say &quot;This is a new version and old lore won't be taken into consideration for future supplements. But the setting is vague enough that if you want to use the old lore instead, you can.&quot;. Instead, the messaging we got was &quot;If you like the old lore, this game isn't for you.&quot;.<br /> <br /> And now it seems like the Renegade-supplements might try to push W5 back into the V5-lane of being somewhat of a continuation. There will be people who similar to the people who think the Onyx Path supplements for V5 aren't &quot;real V5&quot; will consider this direction to also not be &quot;real W5&quot;. Makes you wonder why they changed course. Did the W5 corebook sales disappoint so now Paradox wants to see some course-correction? Or does the Renegade-team just have a different vision for W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just the case of several different line heads with very different marching orders mixed with a lot of freedom for writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T06:45:54-08:00","id":1532157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532150#post1532150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha! Try telling that to Paradox... There's a reason you don't see any more new official releases for 20th Anniversary and CofD.<br /> <br /> I agree with you, though. The WOD-brand would've been better served by keeping 20th and CofD and giving themselves room to truly embrace their specific new 5E-take on the WOD. Also, they should've learned from CofD and there should've been a stronger push for H5 and W5 to stay consistent in their similarities with V5 in the same way games in CofD share similarities.<br /> <br /> But alas, here we are instead, with WOD5E possibly going through yet another shift in direction again</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the only reason I have any interest in WOD5 is because it's a living setting. I only cared about WOD20 at the end when it started advancing the metaplot and characterization again.<br /> <br /> They were fantastic books but I already had the older versions of lore.<br /> <br /> It's a shame OPP didn't get a chance to do more books for W20 but Icons of Rage is what I wanted most of and, of course, it's fantastic and should have been a fully hardback W5 supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T10:41:29-08:00","id":1532173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532145#post1532145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be a bit optimistic, maybe some of the writers came in saying that they couldn't really figure out how to continue the story? Since the book put a hard limit on what one COULD do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Boss: &quot;Alright, it seems like W5 is a bit too low on material. What could we do to add content?<br /> <br /> Employee 1: &quot;Make them suffer from the Avatar Storm!&quot;<br /> <br /> Employee 2: &quot;Have the Cult of Fenris brainwash people like in Danganronpa!&quot;<br /> <br /> Employee 3: &quot;Continuity with the source material.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Boss glares at Employee 3, kicks them out of window)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T12:41:32-08:00","id":1532180,"title":"","content":"But yes, I am probably also setting myself up for disappointment. They're more likely to do Loresheets for old lore and something completely new for everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T18:08:52-08:00","id":1532217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532144#post1532144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>It also didn't help that all the vague blank spaces of the W5 corebook wasn't used to say &quot;This is a new version and old lore won't be taken into consideration for future supplements. But the setting is vague enough that if you want to use the old lore instead, you can.&quot;</b>. Instead, the messaging we got was &quot;If you like the old lore, this game isn't for you.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually fan supplement with that exact same premise as the bolded text called Werewolf the Essentials I've seen floated around tumblr a while back. From what I've read on the main author's blog about the game there's more elements of legacy since there's mention of breeds (humonid, lupis and Crinos born) along some new concepts such as the tribes being divided into different political blocs and the bitten.<br /> <br /> The Main author has opened up a Ko-fi so fans can support the game. PM me if you want a link since the site doesn't seems to like links.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532144#post1532144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes you wonder why they changed course. Did the W5 corebook sales disappoint so now Paradox wants to see some course-correction? Or does the Renegade-team just have a different vision for W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Back on topic I suspect the reason Renegade want's to bring back at least the Albrecht linage since it's mentioned in the core book and well if there's any thing that need clarification it's impotent linages since the werewolf tribe whose whole stick is linage won't actually work well in the core book.<br /> <br /> Well I think we should wait and see how Renegade actually implement the old lore...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T01:50:26-08:00","id":1532234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532217#post1532217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's actually fan supplement with that exact same premise as the bolded text called Werewolf the Essentials I've seen floated around tumblr a while back. From what I've read on the main author's blog about the game there's more elements of legacy since there's mention of breeds (humonid, lupis and Crinos born) along some new concepts such as the tribes being divided into different political blocs and the bitten.<br /> <br /> The Main author has opened up a Ko-fi so fans can support the game. PM me if you want a link since the site doesn't seems to like links.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mundus has some really cool ideas how to handle that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532217#post1532217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on topic I suspect the reason Renegade want's to bring back at least the Albrecht linage since it's mentioned in the core book and well if there's any thing that need clarification it's impotent linages since the werewolf tribe whose whole stick is linage won't actually work well in the core book.<br /> <br /> Well I think we should wait and see how Renegade actually implement the old lore...</div> </div> </div> </div>This will be new lore though. There never was a &quot;Albrecht Lineage&quot; in old Werewolf. Jonas Albrecht got his name from his father. Both his parents were kinfolk, and his Grandfather was a part of a legendary line of heroes who shared the name Morningkill. All of the above were members of House Wyrmfoe. Thus, the Albrecht we know was the first bearer of the Silver Crown and there was no lineage behind him that bore the Crown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T11:23:28-08:00","id":1532245,"title":"","content":"Seriously. After all the strange cut from past lore what is Albrecht doing there? Bait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T18:05:09-08:00","id":1532267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532234#post1532234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mundus has some really cool ideas how to handle that.</div> </div> </div> </div> yep and they plan on writing five whole books of material, which practically speaking is a whole fan gameline.<br /> I'm really interested in seeing how they hold up with the Renegade supplements...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532245#post1532245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously. After all the strange cut from past lore what is Albrecht doing there? Bait?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, it probably some combination of writing team given no direction on how to advance w5 story and the fact the supplement seems to have a focus on a werewolf Lineage so the supplement author have to pick a Recognisable name...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T01:46:10-08:00","id":1532276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532267#post1532267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, it probably some combination of writing team given no direction on how to advance w5 story and the fact the supplement seems to have a focus on a werewolf Lineage so the supplement author have to pick a Recognisable name...</div> </div> </div> </div>The situation is that you had one writing-team for the W5 corebook (the in-house WOD-writing-team at Paradox) which mentioned the &quot;Albrecht lineage&quot; within the Silver-Crown-sidebar. That's the only time the name Albrecht comes up. Now in this supplement you have a different writing-team (the one at Renegade) who has decided to bring back Jonas Albrecht as an individual character.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T13:04:41-08:00","id":1532296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532245#post1532245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously. After all the strange cut from past lore what is Albrecht doing there? Bait?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's just be glad and hope they add more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T17:39:24-08:00","id":1532305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532296#post1532296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's just be glad and hope they add more.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1yTuPFeaD3U\" data-code=\"1yTuPFeaD3U\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1yTuPFeaD3U/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T18:54:02-08:00","id":1532307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532305#post1532305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1yTuPFeaD3U\" data-code=\"1yTuPFeaD3U\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1yTuPFeaD3U/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Why yes that's why you should look forward to Werewolf the Essentials <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T22:47:26-08:00","id":1532316,"title":"","content":"I've still not picked up the W5 book, despite both W20 and Forsaken having survived my last cull (V5 did not, I needed the space for V20). There's just little about WoD5 that feels strange, including the tone being all over the place. This book could theoretically solve W5's issues, but I don't think it would solve my issues with WoD5.<br /> <br /> They've released three games, and they feel restrictive while being all over the place. They also want to explore issues and power structures but seem hesitant to let you step into the shoes of those creating the problem.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is bad and backwards, so they kicked you out.<br /> <br /> Hunter orgs are bad, so you can't join them.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation is bad, thus it destroyed itself in a blaze of uncertainty.<br /> <br /> I think the Cult of Fenris are the apex of this. They're Doing It Wrong, but instead of being told to ask 'why' you're told to kill them without guilt. As if the best way to deal with difficulties and differing beliefs is to sanitize it, give a position, and tell people that any other position is wrong.<br /> <br /> Honestly I don't care about the lore, I want a game that tells me that fighting to change the systems society inflicts on me is right, that rage can be channeled to greater ends, and that a fight against a seemingly insurmountable for might just be possible.<br /> <br /> And I want a game that's willing to say 'discrimination because you were &quot;born wrong&quot; is fucking stupid'. The Crinos born were an ugly element of legacy WtA, but the discomfort they brought had a purpose. W5 threw out all the statements of WtA and replaced them with 'don't go too overboard with your activism'. You're not the Crinos born who's had to endure life as a symbol of shame, and you're also not the Homids who were at the very least complicit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T23:12:50-08:00","id":1532318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <di