ng it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I feel like I can love WtA without spending money, except maybe on W20 books. Still got an incomplete connection, and I've not no desire to support W5 in the slightest.<br /> <br /> But I do wish them well on their project, anyone who wants to make something should not be torn down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T09:30:36-07:00","id":1532332,"title":"","content":"I know I'm late for the talk, and I will read everything posted so far, but I just need to express my shock at... That's it? The Garou Nation is no more? Just like that?<br /> <br /> I'll look into it, but as it stands, it seems that this is an entirely new game instead of &quot;Werewolf the Apocalypse&quot;.<br /> <br /> Much like V5...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T09:52:37-07:00","id":1532334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1531920#post1531920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad you're happy with your purchase and found a game you enjoy. However, there is a very clear strain in the community between people who disliked what Werewolf used to be and are happy with what was served up as W5, and the rest of us who feel that it gutted the soul of the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I never like WtA - nothing against it, in fact I always thought it to be a solid game, just not my cup of tea. But despite that, I recognize that it was a very grounded and well made game.<br /> <br /> And I agree, W5 gutted it's very soul.<br /> <br /> God, I hope they don't make a M5...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T10:16:20-07:00","id":1532335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532334#post1532334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never like WtA - nothing against it, in fact I always thought it to be a solid game, just not my cup of tea. But despite that, I recognize that it was a very grounded and well made game.<br /> <br /> And I agree, W5 gutted it's very soul.<br /> <br /> God, I hope they don't make a M5...</div> </div> </div> </div>They were outlining it when Justin Achilli left. It's difficult to make a single prediction about how badly it could go, because there are just so many ways that it could happen getting compressed and sliced into V5's style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T10:31:51-07:00","id":1532336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532335#post1532335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were outlining it when Justin Achilli left. It's difficult to make a single prediction about how badly it could go, because there are just so many ways that it could happen getting compressed and sliced into V5's style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is it that they felt the need to destroy WoD... Again... And create yet another version of &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot;?<br /> <br /> I mean, WoD has fans. Fans who like WoD.<br /> <br /> Sure, there's some changes that could be done, and some that the fanbase would welcome.<br /> <br /> But why ditching it all in favor of something that clearly ISN'T WoD?<br /> <br /> I mean, it's ok to print a new game... Just give it a new name. &quot;Stories under Darkness&quot;. Now go ahead and &quot;reimagine&quot; it as much as you'd like, instead of making this mess<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T10:48:50-07:00","id":1532337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532157#post1532157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, the only reason I have any interest in WOD5 is because it's a living setting. I only cared about WOD20 at the end when it started advancing the metaplot and characterization again.<br /> <br /> They were fantastic books but I already had the older versions of lore.<br /> <br /> It's a shame OPP didn't get a chance to do more books for W20 but Icons of Rage is what I wanted most of and, of course, it's fantastic and should have been a fully hardback W5 supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm literally the opposite. I don't care about metaplot at all. WoD20 is my favorite because it &quot;cleans up&quot; the mess that were previous editions into one single core book.<br /> <br /> I remember the days when &quot;Vampire the Masquerade&quot; was about a club of 7 clans, while there were also some &quot;boggiemen&quot; called &quot;Sabbath&quot; (whatever the hell those were) and some mysterious &quot;independents&quot;, and there were only some vague descriptions about the sorts of monstrous powers they could have.<br /> <br /> Then I had to get the &quot;Players Guide&quot; to look at some of those &quot;not in the Camarilla&quot;, describing the other clans (except for the Tzimisce and Lasombra) as well as the mythical disciplines above 10, and then finally the &quot;Guide to the Sabbath&quot;... Which took away much of the mystery and mystic about it, but there you have it... <br /> <br /> And the same held true about all lines. In order to get the &quot;full picture&quot;, you needed a dozen of supplements with the information you wanted dispersed throughout them all, most of the times in very disconnected ways <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe 20th to me was the best of the organizers in the world. Sure there was a few things here and there that I still prefered from previous editions, and in those few nitpicks I have I just simply revert back to what I like, but in my opinion the 20th editions were the best in organizing everything about the setting, with all the really important information in the core books and without missing anything vital in them, and supplements are that, supplements, instead of &quot;vitals&quot;. So to me, the 20th editions are the absolute best because it gives it all in a coherent and organized manner and it even corrects and improves many of the problems from previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T11:07:31-07:00","id":1532340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532331#post1532331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I feel like I can love WtA without spending money, except maybe on W20 books. Still got an incomplete connection, and I've not no desire to support W5 in the slightest.<br /> <br /> But I do wish them well on their project, anyone who wants to make something should not be torn down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you're intrested that aspect this project doesn't actually use the W5 system. It uses minds eye threater werewolf the apocalypse which is a completely different system to W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-10-2024, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T13:06:34-07:00","id":1532348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532340#post1532340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you're intrested that aspect this project doesn't actually use the W5 system. It uses minds eye threater werewolf the apocalypse which is a completely different system to W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>It uses W20 as the mechanical baseline. It uses quite a number of elements from the MET Werewolf storyline and some cues for GIft design and organisation from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T17:29:33-07:00","id":1532354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532332#post1532332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm late for the talk, and I will read everything posted so far, but I just need to express my shock at... That's it? The Garou Nation is no more? Just like that?<br /> <br /> I'll look into it, but as it stands, it seems that this is an entirely new game instead of &quot;Werewolf the Apocalypse&quot;.<br /> <br /> Much like V5...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou Nation being gone is old news. It got in the way of the personal horror stuff which was never the point of Werewolf, so it had to go.<br /> <br /> W5 is, like H5, a game to give V5 players a break. Probably a longer one than H5, which doesn't even include a horror creation system, but igt's primarily designed for those who enjoyed being vampires but now want someething a little different. M5 will be the same, and probably with some justification to break apart the traditions, strip away a lot of their powers, and make the Technocracy into straight up villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T19:02:04-07:00","id":1532355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532354#post1532354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Garou Nation being gone is old news. It got in the way of the personal horror stuff which was never the point of Werewolf, so it had to go.<br /> <br /> W5 is, like H5, a game to give V5 players a break. Probably a longer one than H5, which doesn't even include a horror creation system, but igt's primarily designed for those who enjoyed being vampires but now want someething a little different. M5 will be the same, and probably with some justification to break apart the traditions, strip away a lot of their powers, and make the Technocracy into straight up villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean there W:TE which uses W20 derived system and apparently has a stronger continuity with old lore.<br /> <br /> Edit: And well this fandom is niece enough that voting with your wallet could actually be effective...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-10-2024, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T19:58:13-07:00","id":1532356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532355#post1532355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean there W:TE which uses W20 derived system and apparently has a stronger continuity with old lore.<br /> <br /> Edit: And well this fandom is niece enough that voting with your wallet could actually be effective...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're very insistent that I back this one project.<br /> <br /> However that had little to do with the actual post you quoted, which was more to do with Paradox treating anything apart from Vampire as 'a side dish to your main diet of Vampire'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T21:07:46-07:00","id":1532358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532356#post1532356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you're very insistent that I back this one project.<br /> <br /> However that had little to do with the actual post you quoted, which was more to do with Paradox treating anything apart from Vampire as 'a side dish to your main diet of Vampire'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's exactly the problem I and most of the WTA fandom has with Paradox, as you said, they seem insist to every game to follow the VTM formula even if it doesn't fit the gamelines tone.<br /> <br /> Fun fact the reason WTA is so different from VTM is because white wolf realized that the first version of what would become WTA basically involves playing furry Vampire and decided ro go in a different direction, unlike Paradox.<br /> <br /> Like I could get Paradoxes apprch to gamelines if they want to make the fabled &quot;one world of darkness&quot; amd have a cohesive macanical throughline. But it obvious that W5 was intended to be a completely separate thing and would require massive reworking of the Lore to fit into V5.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I want people to look for alternatives to W5 because it's obvious Paradox don't want to make the game WTA fandom wants and hey maybe our funds could make them listen to us and start printing more w20 books.<br /> <br /> Hell if anyone wants W5 done right then they should check out the <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ec258PrLWeU0F-Yy6tUy6lmkTVtX7Rud/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf Punk Remix</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T00:53:49-07:00","id":1532362,"title":"","content":"Paradox isn't going to care if more people by alternatives-to-W5 stuff on STV than people buy W5 stuff. Despite the 20th edition books proving very conclusively that the WoD and CofD not only coexist but actually compliment each other (both on the design side of things, and a healthier community that was fairly well into recovering from the schism created by the original cancelling of the WoD and introduction of the nWoD-that-would-become-CofD), Paradox has effectively cancelled the CofD (so we can't vote with our wallets effectively) If they just stopped approving CofD books completely over competition with the WoD5e, I don't see why they wouldn't delist things in the STV instead of changing W5.<br /> <br /> And while I appreciate the hard work people are putting into things, they don't deserve my money just for it (nor am I inclined to give Paradox money since Paradox gets a cut out of any STV sales for WoD products too). I already have my own WtA collection, and WtF collection, and folder full of house rules, so I can run the Werewolf games I want to run. My smaller play groups don't want to deal with the BNS setting changes any more than the W5 ones. They don't want to have to relearn a bunch of things they already know. We can do things like change the names and make the games more friendly to diverse players already.... we've been doing it or decades. Trying to recruit an online game only gets harder the more you diverge from the official material too.<br /> <br /> More power to people putting their personal work out there, but please, stop. This isn't a thread for &quot;favorite WtA alternative rule sets.&quot; A lot of us might like, enjoy, and at least steal some stuff from those projects for our personal games; but you've already probably crossed the line into turning people off of them by virtue of shilling so hard for them when nobody asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T06:44:41-07:00","id":1532373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532332#post1532332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm late for the talk, and I will read everything posted so far, but I just need to express my shock at... That's it? The Garou Nation is no more? Just like that?<br /> <br /> I'll look into it, but as it stands, it seems that this is an entirely new game instead of &quot;Werewolf the Apocalypse&quot;.<br /> <br /> Much like V5...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it has fallen. It feels a bit like adding insult to injury that the W5 corebook is really bad at explaining the whole thing as well. When it happened, who was involved, what Garou-society looked like after the fall... all questions that are left unanswered. The first paragraph in the Garou-Nation-section in the W5 corebook (pg 37) is a good indicator of just how vague the descriptions are: &quot;The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia? Because the historical events involved in it date to various times across myriad locations, to say with any certainty is impossible, and even spirits speak of it in terms unsuited to the physical world.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bringing now Jonas Albrecht back as a character the PCs can talk to introduces a lot of specificities the W5 corebook actively avoided with a lot of 'Who-even-knows'-shrugging. For example, the Garou-Nation certainly didn't only exist for a couple of decades when you're talking to the last king of it in the 21st century. The description of the Garou-Nation would be very different if it was actually founded in the 20th century. But this is the level of lackluster worldbuilding this supplement has to work with in describing what it's like for Garou to live in a post-Garou-Nation world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T21:16:50-07:00","id":1532419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532373#post1532373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Yeah, it has fallen. It feels a bit like adding insult to injury that the W5 corebook is really bad at explaining the whole thing as well. When it happened, who was involved, what Garou-society looked like after the fall... all questions that are left unanswered</b>. The first paragraph in the Garou-Nation-section in the W5 corebook (pg 37) is a good indicator of just how vague the descriptions are: &quot;The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia? Because the historical events involved in it date to various times across myriad locations, to say with any certainty is impossible, and even spirits speak of it in terms unsuited to the physical world.&quot;<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean minds eye threater werewolf the apocalypse makes it clear that the nation drifted apart due to the differences in the political viewpoints of the tribes so it was split up into three political blocks.<br /> <br /> sure they have disagreements about the way they fight for gaia but they usually don't fight each other...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532373#post1532373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Bringing now Jonas Albrecht back as a character the PCs can talk to introduces a lot of specificities the W5 corebook actively avoided with a lot of 'Who-even-knows'-shrugging. For example, the Garou-Nation certainly didn't only exist for a couple of decades when you're talking to the last king of it in the 21st century. The description of the Garou-Nation would be very different if it was actually founded in the 20th century. But this is the level of lackluster worldbuilding this supplement has to work with in describing what it's like for Garou to live in a post-Garou-Nation world.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the easiest way forward is trying to retcon in the Lore from the aforementioned minds eye threater werewolf the apocalypse, but it will present new problems...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T06:11:55-07:00","id":1532433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532419#post1532419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean minds eye threater werewolf the apocalypse makes it clear that the nation drifted apart due to the differences in the political viewpoints of the tribes so it was split up into three political blocks.<br /> <br /> sure they have disagreements about the way they fight for gaia but they usually don't fight each other...<br /> <br /> Well the easiest way forward is trying to retcon in the Lore from the aforementioned minds eye threater werewolf the apocalypse, but it will present new problems...</div> </div> </div> </div>But really, that just goes to show... You started with that minds eye theater version who had their updated take on WtA, then you had the Hunters Entertainment version who were inspired by that but had their own take, only for that version to be abandoned as things switched to the in-house-team and they had their own take inspired by the Hunters Entertainment version... and now yet again it seems the Renegade-writers will share their take on the version we got to see in the W5 corebook... Man, what a cursed development-history...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T12:56:25-07:00","id":1532447,"title":"","content":"How remarkably on-brand, eh? (Clearly White Wolf\u2019s successors really should have taken more precautions against letting the World of Darkness leak out from their setting into our reality).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T13:20:49-07:00","id":1532449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532433#post1532433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, that just goes to show... You started with that minds eye theater version who had their updated take on WtA, then you had the Hunters Entertainment version who were inspired by that but had their own take, only for that version to be abandoned as things switched to the in-house-team and they had their own take inspired by the Hunters Entertainment version... and now yet again it seems the Renegade-writers will share their take on the version we got to see in the W5 corebook... Man, what a cursed development-history...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep and I bet my two cents that writers at Renegade is fighting the urge to give the corebook the Black hand treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T18:57:38-07:00","id":1532468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532355#post1532355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean there W:TE which uses W20 derived system and apparently has a stronger continuity with old lore.<br /> <br /> Edit: And well this fandom is niece enough that voting with your wallet could actually be effective...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been voting with my wallet for the entirety of this WoD5. I have no interest of acquiring any single one of these books. And I dread about what's to come for M5...<br /> <br /> That being said, I did exactly the same thing when they decided to nuke WoD for the first time in order to create the CofD. I still refuse as a matter of principle to even look at anything remotely related to it. And I don't care if they are good or not - which by the way, apparently it got pretty good by the way. By I refuse to because they utterly disrespected me as a consumer by the time they came up with the &quot;end of the WoD&quot; and tried to shove their new thing over my throat. Therefore, I made a vow to never ever look into CofD ever. Had they showed consideration and appreciation for their consumers, maybe I would be playing the other line.<br /> <br /> Just the same applies here. I will NEVER EVER look into ANYTHING that comes out of this 5ed line... Even if they improve it to become 10x better than &quot;classic WoD&quot; down the line, because I consider their actions towards me as a consumer to be utterly insulting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T19:06:46-07:00","id":1532469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532373#post1532373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it has fallen. It feels a bit like adding insult to injury that the W5 corebook is really bad at explaining the whole thing as well. When it happened, who was involved, what Garou-society looked like after the fall... all questions that are left unanswered. The first paragraph in the Garou-Nation-section in the W5 corebook (pg 37) is a good indicator of just how vague the descriptions are: &quot;The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia? Because the historical events involved in it date to various times across myriad locations, to say with any certainty is impossible, and even spirits speak of it in terms unsuited to the physical world.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bringing now Jonas Albrecht back as a character the PCs can talk to introduces a lot of specificities the W5 corebook actively avoided with a lot of 'Who-even-knows'-shrugging. For example, the Garou-Nation certainly didn't only exist for a couple of decades when you're talking to the last king of it in the 21st century. The description of the Garou-Nation would be very different if it was actually founded in the 20th century. But this is the level of lackluster worldbuilding this supplement has to work with in describing what it's like for Garou to live in a post-Garou-Nation world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. So they decided to go for full stupidity then. Thanks for the heads up. Now that my curiosity is sated, I can go back to never caring and pretending that this entire 5e thing doesn't exist at all. Thanks a lot.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, when M5 comes out, just brief me up into the amount of stupid of it, I want to laugh a bit before ignoring it completely for the rest of my life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T21:02:49-07:00","id":1532475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532469#post1532469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. So they decided to go for full stupidity then. Thanks for the heads up. Now that my curiosity is sated, I can go back to never caring and pretending that this entire 5e thing doesn't exist at all. Thanks a lot.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, when M5 comes out, just brief me up into the amount of stupid of it, I want to laugh a bit before ignoring it completely for the rest of my life</div> </div> </div> </div>Well see you in the next edition then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T22:40:11-07:00","id":1532482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532468#post1532468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have been voting with my wallet for the entirety of this WoD5. I have no interest of acquiring any single one of these books. And I dread about what's to come for M5...<br /> <br /> That being said, I did exactly the same thing when they decided to nuke WoD for the first time in order to create the CofD. I still refuse as a matter of principle to even look at anything remotely related to it. And I don't care if they are good or not - which by the way, apparently it got pretty good by the way. By I refuse to because they utterly disrespected me as a consumer by the time they came up with the &quot;end of the WoD&quot; and tried to shove their new thing over my throat. Therefore, I made a vow to never ever look into CofD ever. Had they showed consideration and appreciation for their consumers, maybe I would be playing the other line.<br /> <br /> Just the same applies here. I will NEVER EVER look into ANYTHING that comes out of this 5ed line... Even if they improve it to become 10x better than &quot;classic WoD&quot; down the line, because I consider their actions towards me as a consumer to be utterly insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit extreme, CofD got great when it started being incredibly <i>different</i> to WoD. I do highly recommend looking at the lines which don't have an equivalent in WoD, especially Deviant, but honestly still outright refusing to look at the books because the developers of WoD ended it in the way they wanted is quite frankly showing a lack of respect for the creatives.<br /> <br /> Which is the thing, WW did something pretty amazing by ending it on a high instead of letting it suffer heat death. They could have done a lot better with the followup, remaking the games (especially Vampire) was the wrong move, but there's a definite level of integrity in the way they ended everything.<br /> <br /> Although I do understand, I'm still trying to burn Age of Sigmar with fire.<br /> <br /> Honestly the biggest issue is not the lack of respect WW has shown for the consumers, but their haphazard approach to the property and lack of nrespect for the people making it. Something something Swords of Heimdall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T03:00:21-07:00","id":1532485,"title":"","content":"Could someone explain to me one thing cause I do not understand something.<br /> Apocalyptic Record is very fine book with tons of ideas. Very good ideas for campaigns. An there is W5 with concepts in conflict with AR ideas.<br /> Why? Second thing - the company is trying to not step on any toes and make the most polite game and at the same W5 is excluding Get, Stargazers, metis, lupus ... Is it even normal?<br /> Ther will be always someone disappointed by book. But they turned the wrong turn. For example. Few words from AR made me understand why the Wendigo tribe name should be changed while a lot of official and forum materials did not. Some changes made were unnecessary. I hope that we can get an opportunity to play Get, metis and other... Cause isn't it cancel culture personificated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 03-13-2024, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T03:34:19-07:00","id":1532486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532485#post1532485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone explain to me one thing cause I do not understand something.<br /> Apocalyptic Record is very fine book with tons of ideas. Very good ideas for campaigns. An there is W5 with concepts in conflict with AR ideas.<br /> Why? Second thing - the company is trying to not step on any toes and make the most polite game and at the same W5 is excluding Get, Stargazers, metis, lupus ... Is it even normal?<br /> Ther will be always someone disappointed by book. But they turned the wrong turn. For example. Few words from AR made me understand why the Wendigo tribe name should be changed while a lot of official and forum materials did not. Some changes made were unnecessary. I hope that we can get an opportunity to play Get, metis and other... Cause isn't it cancel culture personificated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apocalyptic Record is in no way related to W5. W5 is a reboot and a reimagining - there never was the storyline of the old Werewolf in the history of W5. It's exactly what's in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T04:09:31-07:00","id":1532489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532485#post1532485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone explain to me one thing cause I do not understand something.<br /> Apocalyptic Record is very fine book with tons of ideas. Very good ideas for campaigns. An there is W5 with concepts in conflict with AR ideas.<br /> Why? Second thing - the company is trying to not step on any toes and make the most polite game and at the same W5 is excluding Get, Stargazers, metis, lupus ... Is it even normal?<br /> Ther will be always someone disappointed by book. But they turned the wrong turn. For example. Few words from AR made me understand why the Wendigo tribe name should be changed while a lot of official and forum materials did not. Some changes made were unnecessary. I hope that we can get an opportunity to play Get, metis and other... Cause isn't it cancel culture personificated?</div> </div> </div> </div>At some point when development switched to the in-house team at Paradox, this idea of &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; was adopted for the released version. Here's a bit from the Discord Q&amp;A that Justin Achilli did back in October 2022 which talks about this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Which playable Tribe has gone through the most changes?</b><br /> It's less about &quot;changes from&quot; and more about remaining true to its own edition. No event happened in the diegetic world that made the W5 era occur, so it's better to think of it as a clean break that intends to remain consistent with itself rather than legacy editions. </div> </div> </div>So, unlike with V5, the messaging for W5 has been that it isn't connected to the previous editions. But of course, the main-topic of this thread is that this supplement re-introducing Jonas Albrecht kinda goes against that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T04:57:05-07:00","id":1532491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532489#post1532489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So, unlike with V5, the messaging for W5 has been that it isn't connected to the previous editions. But of course, the main-topic of this thread is that this supplement re-introducing Jonas Albrecht kinda goes against that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly It could just be the result of Renegade authors trying to find any material to put into the supplment regardless of the intent of the corebook due to the fact that the lead writer left.<br /> <br /> Honestly with the dysfunction Ive seen with the development of the gameline I won't be surprised if Paradox drops Renegade games shortly after all they supplements are delivered and replace them with I don't know Sanguine Games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-13-2024, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T05:22:08-07:00","id":1532493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532491#post1532491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly It could just be the result of Renegade authors trying to find any material to put into the supplment regardless of the intent of the corebook due to the fact that the lead writer left.<br /> <br /> Honestly with the dysfunction Ive seen with the development of the gameline I won't be surprised if Paradox drops Renegade games shortly after all they supplements are delivered and replace them with I don't know Sanguine Games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, of course, it's speculation but my prediction is the exact opposite: They'll disband the in-house Paradox-team and just give the development of the RPG-books completely to Renegade (both supplements <i>and </i>corebooks). Paradox just deciding to completely sideline the RPG-book-angle of the license and focus on videogames instead. But I think a lot of this is riding on the upcoming Bloodlines 2 and what happens with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T07:03:51-07:00","id":1532496,"title":"","content":"I'd be glad if Renegade took the whole game and fix the bad ideas.with upcoming supplements.<br /> i hoped that Apocalyptic Record would be some bridge between editions but it's not. It's different boom but still with very good ideas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T11:16:30-07:00","id":1532515,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm curious to see is if those who have no tribe are addressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T12:04:11-07:00","id":1532517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532489#post1532489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, unlike with V5, the messaging for W5 has been that it isn't connected to the previous editions. But of course, the main-topic of this thread is that this supplement re-introducing Jonas Albrecht kinda goes against that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It coukd just be reusing a character name and concept, we'll just have to wait and see. I wouldn't be shocked if they were told to include the last king of the Garou Nation and thought 'well might ad well call him Jonas Albrecht'.<br /> <br /> More likely though it's probably a cynnical attempt to pretend they're 'fixing' W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T12:47:44-07:00","id":1532519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532493#post1532493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think a lot of this is riding on the upcoming Bloodlines 2 and what happens with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the feeling that Paradox putting the future of a large part of they product line in the hands of a game with an equally troubled development history as w5 isn't going to go well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T19:51:53-07:00","id":1532533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532482#post1532482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a bit extreme, CofD got great when it started being incredibly <i>different</i> to WoD. I do highly recommend looking at the lines which don't have an equivalent in WoD, especially Deviant, but honestly still outright refusing to look at the books because the developers of WoD ended it in the way they wanted is quite frankly showing a lack of respect for the creatives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At the time of the &quot;End of the World&quot; of WoD, I made to vow to myself to NEVER look at the &quot;New World of Darkness&quot;. And I always take my words very seriously. I'm not the kind of man that ever backtracks on my words. Thus, I will not, never ever, look a CofD. Oh and don't make any mistakes, from all the news and small pieces of comments that I heard about here and there, I am 100% sure that it is a great line; maybe, possibly even better than WoD itself.<br /> <br /> But I don't care. I don't care if it is absolutely awesome. Fool me once, shame on you. Fool me twice, shame on me. I'm not a Christian, &quot;forgiveness&quot; absolutely is not on my DNA. So, I refuse to look at any one of these books, and I had personal friends who invited me to play them and I refused them, and there's nothing anyone can say me to convince me otherwise. They disrespected me once, with me there's no second round, there's no second chance.<br /> <br /> But hey, I'm not trying to trash on CofD, quite the opposite, I'm sure it is a great line. I just simply don't want to have anything to do with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is the thing, WW did something pretty amazing by ending it on a high instead of letting it suffer heat death. They could have done a lot better with the followup, remaking the games (especially Vampire) was the wrong move, but there's a definite level of integrity in the way they ended everything.<br /> <br /> Although I do understand, I'm still trying to burn Age of Sigmar with fire.<br /> <br /> Honestly the biggest issue is not the lack of respect WW has shown for the consumers, but their haphazard approach to the property and lack of nrespect for the people making it. Something something Swords of Heimdall. </div> </div> </div>Nah, they did disrespect everybody, not just for the people making, but mostly to the fans/consumers. What they did was trying to tell us, the players, the fans, the consumers &quot;look, WoD is done, it's toast, quit whining about it and buy this new stuff instead&quot;. They insulted us by trying to shove it down our throats, in the very same manner that they are doing with this 5ed (except that what they did was worse), and I simply refuse to accept that, and so I remain as immovable as a rock on my stance. I'll never look at any CofD books, and I have been living happily ever after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 03-13-2024, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T20:39:05-07:00","id":1532534,"title":"","content":"While I get nothing we say is going to change your mind.... is there a reason you keep seeming to want to talk about it?<br /> <br /> Because it mostly feels like you want to rant about something that has more holes than Swiss cheese in its reasoning while proactively trying to shut up anyone that would point out all those holes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T21:05:41-07:00","id":1532537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532533#post1532533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I'm not a Christian, &quot;forgiveness&quot; absolutely is not on my DNA. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow calming that a religion came up with a emotion is the most r/atheist take I've seen in a long time.<br /> <br /> So Uh moving on...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532533#post1532533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They insulted us by trying to shove it down our throats, in the very same manner that they are doing with this 5ed (except that what they did was worse), and I simply refuse to accept that, and so I remain as immovable as a rock on my stance. I'll never look at any CofD books, and I have been living happily ever after.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually suspect that 5e might not be long for this would if Bloodlines 2 flops since apparently Pardox is moving resources to video game production and if they flagship game fail then I can see three possibilities:<br /> 1. paradox shutter all production and planning of all WOD content and do some &quot;Restructuring&quot; for an unknown amount of time<br /> 2. paradox decides to do what GW did with the Warhammer: 40K and hands their IP to anyone who can pay a relatively low fee to make what ever they want with it<br /> 3. Paradox decides to pivot to CYOA games and maybe table top games since they cheap and Paradox wants to recover something from this mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T21:13:48-07:00","id":1532538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532537#post1532537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow calming that a religion came up with a emotion is the most r/atheist take I've seen in a long time.<br /> <br /> So Uh moving on...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not trying to insult Christianism or Christians - quite the opposite in fact. I admire their teachings and their capacity to forgive. But I sadly, am completely incapable of. That's a major character flaw that I have and I fully and unapologetically admit it, but alas, it is what is. I'm incapable of forgiving, so I had to learn to live with that. A salute the Christians and non Christians who can, because that is beyond me, so I envy those who manage to do it.<br /> <br /> PS: I also have no trouble admitting that being an atheist is no panacea. I would probably be happier and have a better life if I were a believer, even if it's a &quot;noble lie&quot;. What say you, what do you think it's better, the blue pill or the red pill? Sweet illusions or the harsh reality? That's a hard choice.<br /> <br /> And I'm getting older and reading a lot of Nietzsche, I'm beginning to agree with him on many many things... We are so obsessed with the &quot;truth&quot;, and the truth may not be that important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 03-14-2024, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T21:42:59-07:00","id":1532540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532538#post1532538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's obvious that you seem to be dealing with some heavy stuff and I don't think being on this forum would improve you're mood much. So I uh suggest we move on and talk about something else like how screwed w5 if not the whole 5e is screwed if Bloodlines 2 flops hard enough...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T22:03:18-07:00","id":1532542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532540#post1532540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it's obvious that you seem to be dealing with some heavy stuff and I don't think being on this forum would improve you're mood much. So I uh suggest we move on and talk about something else like how screwed w5 if not the whole 5e is screwed if Bloodlines 2 flops hard enough...</div> </div> </div> </div>This 5ed is trash. Lets no mingle words here, and let us call it for what it is: IT IS TRASH.<br /> <br /> This can't possibly have a future, simply because it is pure garbage. WoD has always been a flawed masterpiece, and it had been improving constantly over the years. It had problems? Yes. But it was awesome despite those small rough edges - like a raw diamond.<br /> <br /> But this? Any effort towards this is like trying to polish fecal matter. The only thing that will come out of it is just more shit.<br /> <br /> And the reason is simple: they have no love, no passion, for what they have. The original WoD game lines were like raw explosions of Glamour; sometimes chaotic, sometimes even nonsensical and laughably silly, but in a good and honest way.<br /> <br /> But this? This is just pure Banality. This &quot;5th edition&quot; is just pure Banality, it is dull and unimaginative and has no passion to it, just quotas to be reached under a timetable of a bureocratic hierarchy. It has no future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T22:57:08-07:00","id":1532546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532542#post1532542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, oh right enough of this depressing bullshit!<br /> <br /> I know 5e is trash. Like the best future I can picture for this project is Paradox selling the IP to half a dozen shovel-ware phone game devs and hope that some of them can put out a half decent product. The more likely outcome would be them comssing a few cyoa books then getting IP out back to be shot.<br /> <br /> And god forbid that you don't look for something else than 5e, like chronicles of darkness, which despite you're stubborn belief isn't a replacement for WOD for a LOOONG time and it's all the better for it.<br /> <br /> If chronicles isn't palatable for you then you could try 20th anniversary editions or hell burvia's hunter the parenting where from what little we've seen of they version of the WOD setting is much more compelling than 5e.<br /> <br /> Or hell maybe you want something more out there like the whole Project Moon Shared Universe which as far as I know is WOD earth after it was hit by ALL the apocalypses across the game lines hit it (Don't fight me on this!!!) and whatever the hells Curseborne is.<br /> <br /> But I suspect that you aren't satisfied with any of those answers I provided since as far as I know You use this thread as an excuse to post rants about you're life disguised as criticisms.<br /> <br /> Dude get some rest, talk to someone, TOUCH SOME GOD DAMN GRASS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-14-2024, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T06:11:25-07:00","id":1532568,"title":"","content":"I agree that Fifth Edition is flawed, but am reluctant to accept such an all-consuming dismissal: optimism can be a powerful drug!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T07:36:52-07:00","id":1532576,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\">MrornX</a></b> and <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\">Magus Maximus</a></b>\u200b <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#8B0000\"><b>Let's tone it down a bit. This is getting a little too heated. Both of you, please take a little time from the topic to reframe your approach and refrain from attacking one another.</b></span></span></span>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T10:24:53-07:00","id":1532586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532568#post1532568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree that Fifth Edition is flawed, but am reluctant to accept such an all-consuming dismissal: optimism can be a powerful drug!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also V5 wasn't that bad. Heavily flawed, but more than passable as a game about vampires politicking.<br /> <br /> H5 and W5 made me give my V5 books to a charity shop, but I hope they both do have an audience who likes them. Heck, I like MCWoD, there's an audience out there for every game. The only question is if Paradox found that audience.<br /> <br /> Now I'm just waiting until I have the free paycheque for more WoD20 and CofD books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T11:35:19-07:00","id":1532590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532568#post1532568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree that Fifth Edition is flawed, but am reluctant to accept such an all-consuming dismissal: optimism can be a powerful drug!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is in a good place right now, I would say. It started with a flawed corebook but there are so many supplements out at this point that it's fairly easy to find inspiration for adding mechanics and adjusting things here and there in the game. Also, bringing back old lore isn't too hard.<br /> <br /> But H5 and W5 on the other hand... I think mechanically W5 at least is workable if you go along with the depressing take on Garou but the lore/worldbuilding is terrible in my opinion. H5, though... Man, that's an all-around bad game. Mind you, the newly announced supplement Incognito Report introduces some much-needed elements to H5 like, for example, how exactly the Danger-Track is supposed to work. It's a core-mechanic of the game and the corebook only offers various examples with no basis for how it should work. It isn't even a &quot;game-mechanic&quot; in the strictest sense since it's 100% ST-fiat. The first supplement Lines Drawn By Blood, for example, with its pre-planned Chronicles tells readers when the &quot;mechanics&quot; described in the corebook for the increase in the Danger-track apply, when they should be ignored and how STs should artificially keep the Danger-Track-rating at a certain level depending in which chapter of the Chronicle the PCs are.<br /> <br /> The thing with both the H5 and the W5 corebook is that I still don't understand why both books looked at the V5 corebook and said &quot;Let's do less than that.&quot;. Of course, those likely weren't the exact words or goals for developing these two corebooks but that's what came out in the end. Like with Pack-Types in the case of this supplement or offering concrete guidelines for the Danger-Track in the case of the H5 supplement Incognito-Report, these are things that should've been in the corebook. And not just because these are neat additions but because the V5 corebook managed to cover stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T12:10:19-07:00","id":1532598,"title":"","content":"It's also kinda weird because while V5 is a book with a significantly higher page count than H5 or W5, it also has a highly inefficient layout style (that H5 and W5 dropped for something closer to traditional WW looking books) that basically added ~100 pages. IIRC in terms of word count, V5 and W5 are fairly close to each other... making the amount of stuff covered or not covered kinda baffling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T13:37:29-07:00","id":1532605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532598#post1532598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also kinda weird because while V5 is a book with a significantly higher page count than H5 or W5, it also has a highly inefficient layout style (that H5 and W5 dropped for something closer to traditional WW looking books) that basically added ~100 pages. IIRC in terms of word count, V5 and W5 are fairly close to each other... making the amount of stuff covered or not covered kinda baffling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the easiest answer is to sell supplements. Despite what the corebook author said or intended, the blank spaces in the book will be filled in by supplements sooner or later...<br /> <br /> Also appenly a H5 supplemet actually goes against the corebook themes what with that? and what does that say about Shattered nation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-14-2024, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T19:10:38-07:00","id":1532629,"title":"","content":"V5 has a bunch of supplements, so I'm not sure that really scans. The 2e and Revised WoD corebooks are, again in terms of word count, about the same quantity as V5 and W5... and they managed to pump out tons of supplements. The massive tomes of V20, W20, and M20 also have considerable numbers of supplements (and besides V20, most of the 20th games would probably have more books if not for Paradox's interference).<br /> <br /> The desire to sell supplements just doesn't explain anything here: You need solid enough corebooks that people want supplements to expand on what the corebook establishes, so getting more sparse in the cores doesn't help sell more books. You need supplements that expand instead of contradict the corebooks so people want the supplements to aid in the game they bought and want to buy more for.<br /> <br /> TTRPGs don't work like video games where you start with a loss-leader (consoles for video games, despite how incredibly expensive they've become, are not profitable) and then make your money in all the $70 games you sell to play with it. Core books are where the vast majority of the money in TTRPGs are. Even D&amp;D has had to deal with this. The supplement market makes money, but it's greater purpose is keeping customers engaged with your game with new material than not. People that buy lots of supplements are more likely to buy more core books later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T20:56:12-07:00","id":1532634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532629#post1532629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TTRPGs don't work like video games where you start with a loss-leader (consoles for video games, despite how incredibly expensive they've become, are not profitable) and then make your money in all the $70 games you sell to play with it. Core books are where the vast majority of the money in TTRPGs are. Even D&amp;D has had to deal with this. The supplement market makes money, but it's greater purpose is keeping customers engaged with your game with new material than not. People that buy lots of supplements are more likely to buy more core books later.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible that some of the Issues that plagued the 5e line might have come from the higher ups of paradox treating the supplements like DLCs for they games instead of stand alone books that references the core book. The problem is compounded by paradox purging most of the V5 team because they caused a political incident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-15-2024, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T03:16:24-07:00","id":1532640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532605#post1532605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the easiest answer is to sell supplements. Despite what the corebook author said or intended, the blank spaces in the book will be filled in by supplements sooner or later...<br /> <br /> Also appenly a H5 supplemet actually goes against the corebook themes what with that? and what does that say about Shattered nation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. The example I would cite here is the way Justin Achilli talked about developing H5 in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ir6BpM8Fjus\" target=\"_blank\">this interview with Outstar</a>. Now this comes with two caveats: We know that Paradox mandates certain things for WOD5E like the heavy focus on street-level or specific things like de-emphasizing the Umbra in W5. But Justin Achilli never made clear to what degree Paradox influenced the development-process. The other thing is that his explanation for why the Get were turned into antagonists turned out to be false, so I guess any statement of his must therefore be taken with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> But the example I specifically have in mind is his idea of &quot;Sober Play&quot;. It's the idea that all the other splats are controlled by some force, the Beast in the case of Vampire, Rage for Werewolf etc. But since H5 is about mortal hunters there is nothing that influences their actions. The characters have essentially free will (unlike a Vampire with Humanity 4 or less, for example). Now that was the idea... What this meant in praxis, though, was that H5 didn't have an equivalent for Humanity and with that the trifecta of things attached to this VtM-mechanic, Convictions, Chronicle-Tenets and Touchstones were also removed and downscaled. Convictions are gone, Chronicle-Tenets no longer influence the game and Touchstones now only matter if a character has none. There's no upside to having Touchstones in H5, only the downside of a character getting punished if they have no Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Of course, you only have to look to the CofD (and specifically Hunter the Vigil) to realize that the answer is to find something equivalent to Humanity that works for mortal hunters (in the case of HtV it's a trait called Integrity) rather than just ditching the concept of a morality-mechanic as a whole. The idea wasn't to say &quot;We're leaving room open for some supplement to fill this space.&quot;, the development-team just decided to reject a key-part of V5's design in the most straightforward manner imaginable - by removing it and replacing it with nothing. Never understood where that impulse came from to reject V5's design like that but it was there.<br /> <br /> Another example, Pack-Types... you'd think it would be a no-brainer to take Coterie-Types and develop something equivalent for W5. Instead, they went with this caern-management-system. And once again, this wasn't a choice of &quot;Let's leave this to the supplements.&quot; because rather the caern-management was giving priority over having something equivalent to Coterie-Types. From pg. 191: &quot;As a game, Werewolf: The Apocalypse assumes that the players\u2019 characters will have their own caern, or that their pack will belong to the sept of a specific caern.&quot;. Instead of the variety Coterie-Types/Pack-Types could potentially offer, W5 instead just <i>&quot;assumes&quot;</i> you gonna end up managing a caern while playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T04:31:36-07:00","id":1532641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532640#post1532640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another example, Pack-Types... you'd think it would be a no-brainer to take Coterie-Types and develop something equivalent for W5. Instead, they went with this caern-management-system. And once again, this wasn't a choice of &quot;Let's leave this to the supplements.&quot; because rather the caern-management was giving priority over having something equivalent to Coterie-Types. From pg. 191: &quot;As a game, Werewolf: The Apocalypse assumes that the players\u2019 characters will have their own caern, or that their pack will belong to the sept of a specific caern.&quot;. Instead of the variety Coterie-Types/Pack-Types could potentially offer, W5 instead just <i>&quot;assumes&quot;</i> you gonna end up managing a caern while playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this takes me back to the days when V5 was playtested and the playtest (aside from its myriad of OTHER issues) was railroady as hell. Like, going through the woods got you killed by garou. No, not combat, an off-screen statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T05:26:40-07:00","id":1532643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532640#post1532640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But the example I specifically have in mind is his idea of &quot;Sober Play&quot;. It's the idea that all the other splats are controlled by some force, the Beast in the case of Vampire, Rage for Werewolf etc. But since H5 is about mortal hunters there is nothing that influences their actions. The characters have essentially free will (unlike a Vampire with Humanity 4 or less, for example). Now that was the idea... What this meant in praxis, though, was that H5 didn't have an equivalent for Humanity and with that the trifecta of things attached to this VtM-mechanic, Convictions, Chronicle-Tenets and Touchstones were also removed and downscaled. Convictions are gone, Chronicle-Tenets no longer influence the game and Touchstones now only matter if a character has none. There's no upside to having Touchstones in H5, only the downside of a character getting punished if they have no Touchstone.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You know in my Version of WOD I would actually de-empathize any supernatural force having influence on the PC's. Like sure Rage and the beast still exists in my version but if managed properly those would be a non-factor in character interaction, my motto for this version WOD &quot;The Mindset makes the Monster&quot;. Hell the hunter equivalent splat explicitly has no Humanity equivalent since well they're already human, they could be as various and savage as any other human.<br /> <br /> The only instance of a supernaturally enforced morale system only comes into play if you're PC endured an very specific instance of trauma that strike at something verry personal to they PC, Shatter they conception of the world, Ect. and even then it would take a lot of failed willpower roll for it to have any effect then you either degrade into a beast that made of that internalized trauma or you gain EGO which is you're very own super-Klaive. And this applies to all the splats in the City since the light from L-corp can affect every thing that's capable of emotion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532640#post1532640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of the variety Coterie-Types/Pack-Types could potentially offer, W5 instead just <i>&quot;assumes&quot;</i> you gonna end up managing a caern while playing.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Funny you should mention that since if you read the first page of this thread Shattered Nation introduces Pack-Types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T01:31:34-07:00","id":1532687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532643#post1532643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know in my Version of WOD I would actually de-empathize any supernatural force having influence on the PC's. Like sure Rage and the beast still exists in my version but if managed properly those would be a non-factor in character interaction, my motto for this version WOD &quot;The Mindset makes the Monster&quot;. Hell the hunter equivalent splat explicitly has no Humanity equivalent since well they're already human, they could be as various and savage as any other human.<br /> <br /> The only instance of a supernaturally enforced morale system only comes into play if you're PC endured an very specific instance of trauma that strike at something verry personal to they PC, Shatter they conception of the world, Ect. and even then it would take a lot of failed willpower roll for it to have any effect then you either degrade into a beast that made of that internalized trauma or you gain EGO which is you're very own super-Klaive. And this applies to all the splats in the City since the light from L-corp can affect every thing that's capable of emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you restart with a blank slate there are lots of ways to go with this. In this case, I think when you get to H5 and W5, you have to orient yourself around what V5 did. It's a constraint, sure. But WOD5E is supposed to be a franchise and hopefully, there's some overlap between people who play one splat also being interested in playing other splats. And so for the sake of accessibility, establishing through-lines like what CofD did, I think, is a good idea.<br /> <br /> And you talking about de-emphasizing gave me an idea: One way, I think, to de-emphasize is to take the whole mechanic and make it happen at the end of every Chapter instead. So rather than tallying all the bad stuff and setbacks and what this means for your Humanity-track at the end of a session or during the game, you do it at the end of the Chapter. That's one way to de-emphasize it in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532643#post1532643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny you should mention that since if you read the first page of this thread Shattered Nation introduces Pack-Types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, what's strange is that in V5 it happened the other way around. The corebook first introduced Coterie-Types and then the V5 Players Guide with its expanded Coterie Creation introduced a more expansive Domain-management-system. But here with W5 they decided to do the territory-management-system first.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T03:28:29-07:00","id":1532694,"title":"","content":"I think what the designers think WoD5 is is a series of games about relationships. Like some kind of adult-focused Monsterhearts. V5 is about you desperately trying to cling onto your human relationships, Hunter is about how your attachment to others drives you to dangerous extremes, and Werewolf is about how your tendency to last out destroys your relationships.<br /> <br /> They're not, any more than cWoD was a game about telling a story. Powered by the Apocalypse is a system basically built around relationships and identity, to the point where sufficient intimacy can significantly shift relative character power. WoD5 just has nothing akin to Strings, at best your meaningful relationships number at 3.<br /> <br /> If I'm right then I suspect W5 might get a course correction to focusing more on proactive defiance. Which the silver crown plot hooks potentially tie into, with it or similar symbols allowing PCs to dangle local caerns into a more united front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T05:06:25-07:00","id":1532698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532687#post1532687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One way, I think, to de-emphasize is to take the whole mechanic and make it happen at the end of every Chapter instead. So rather than tallying all the bad stuff and setbacks and what this means for your Humanity-track at the end of a session or during the game, you do it at the end of the Chapter. That's one way to de-emphasize it in my opinion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I thinking more of a universal sanity meter for all the splats and having mechanics like rage and the beast regulated to supplementary mechanics that only become more trouble some when you get <i>really </i>low on the meter. Normal humans on the other hand just have to deal with good old insanity.<br /> <br /> On that note I would actually separate Touchstone into Contacts and Bonds.<br /> <br /> Contacts is meant represent people who the PC knows and regally meet but don't really have much emotional connection to and they interaction with the PC tend to be for a service or transactional (paying ahn for weapons, trading rumors, Giving the PC missions, paying rent, ect)<br /> <br /> Bonds on the other hand are people that are deeper connection to the PC than Contacts weather via they back story or a Contact getting more familiar the the PC. Bonds take the traditional role of the Touchstone as the link to keep the PC sane, while also providing addition benefits depending on they role (welling ness lone the PC a weapon for a session, Provide free information related to the PC goals, A buff in combat when assisting the pc, ect )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T01:32:46-07:00","id":1532889,"title":"","content":"So somebody on rpg.net reported that he has played the latest adventure you can get from that Renegade-play-program. And guess what's back...? Ancestor-spirits! Also, the human allies of the Garou are a big family that has been in an alliance with the Garou for multiple generations and occasionally members of that bloodline turn into Garou. So, it's pretty much Kinfolk in all but name.<br /> <br /> That kinda confirms the direction things are heading into: These supplements are going to reintroduce old lore/worldbuilding and making W5 more similar to V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T02:38:37-07:00","id":1532892,"title":"","content":"That's still going to end up really strange in-play unless there's a ton of new rules along side of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T03:37:27-07:00","id":1532893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532892#post1532892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's still going to end up really strange in-play unless there's a ton of new rules along side of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or do what the V5 books apparently did and ignore the Corebook mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T03:58:18-07:00","id":1532896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532892#post1532892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's still going to end up really strange in-play unless there's a ton of new rules along side of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not any stranger than when they introduced that Loresheet for these two sisters and they were a Pack with a custom Pack-Patron-Spirit. A thing that currently has no rules in W5. I mean, yeah, they certainly have their work cut out for them if they want to reorient the direction of W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T15:48:25-07:00","id":1532924,"title":"","content":"Yeah....this is totally gonna split the new W5 fan base ( such as it is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T00:48:56-07:00","id":1532934,"title":"","content":"I mean, is this direction they're heading into really worse than &quot;If you're a fan of the previous editions, this isn't for you.&quot;...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T00:59:54-07:00","id":1532935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532934#post1532934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, is this direction they're heading into really worse than &quot;If you're a fan of the previous editions, this isn't for you.&quot;...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Look at Rise of Sky walker and Halo Infinite, doing a 180 in story direction worked out great /s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-21-2024, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T06:01:10-07:00","id":1532939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532935#post1532935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well Look at Rise of Sky walker and Halo Infinite, doing a 180 in story direction worked out great /s</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be sure to shake my head if there's something like &quot;Somehow, the Seventh Generation/Black Tooth/etc. came back to life!&quot;, but this seems more like giving connections required by the context that the core book wanted, but thought that it didn't need to describe. For example, Garou don't have elders like the vampires do; the only way to have ancient, opinionated people that have to be listened to is if you have ancestor-spirits and the Ancestors Background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T06:28:07-07:00","id":1532940,"title":"","content":"It actually would've helped with the vagueness of the corebook if it had tagged itself as the same kind of semi-continuation that V5 is. It would've been strange to not include the Ancestors Background or list Ancestor-Spirits somewhere but just one line about talking to Ancestor-Spirits would've been enough. And even without a line, the messaging that it's still connected to the previous editions somewhat would've made clear &quot;Yep, Ancestor-spirits are still a thing.&quot;.<br /> <br /> But not only was it explicitly not a continuation but the messaging was clear that anything not mentioned wouldn't be part of the W5 setting anymore. After all, that's what happened with the Moonbridges. They weren't just not mentioned, the developers made it clear: Moonbridges don't exist in W5. And so it's justifiable to assume that Ancestor-Spirits had been excluded as well. And yet, now they're back. This makes getting a grip on what parts from previous WtA editions are or aren't part of the W5 setting at this point a bit of a challenge.<br /> <br /> Although the funniest outcome would be for a future Renegade-supplement to bring back Moonbridges as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T09:19:46-07:00","id":1532944,"title":"","content":"All in one hilarity if it all happened in one book! Ancestor-spirits, moon bridges, stepping sideways with only a mirror, survivable Umbra, and the Get of Fenris replacing the Cult! (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T12:28:12-07:00","id":1532951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532935#post1532935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Look at Rise of Sky walker and Halo Infinite, doing a 180 in story direction worked out great /s</div> </div> </div> </div>While I get the sarcastic intent....<br /> <br /> Rise of Skywalker made Disney a giant pile of money. So it did actually work out great for the company. It also think it worked out pretty well for Star Wars fans that they decided to stop trying to do blockbuster epic movies and put way more focus on streaming shows. While the shows have been varied in quality, they're easier to watch on their own, and generally have made the fans happier than the movies getting pulled in four or five different directions by people at the top.<br /> <br /> Probably more importantly, Rise of the Skywalker didn't actually do a 180 on the plot, it did a 180 on the themes in a particularly self-undermining way. A big reveal isn't a change in the direction of the plot, it's a change in the context of the plot. W5 doesn't even have a plot. So it's hard to really compare what the hardcore fan reactions are going to be to Renegade trying to push more legacy material back into W5 despite the original intent for it to be a new take on the game.<br /> <br /> Halo fans generally don't have a problem with Infinite doing a 180 on the plot because it was a course correction of the most hated Halo plot in the previous game, which was a 180 in its own way (totaling in a 360 with a whiff instead of a no scope). Halo Infinite's plot has problems, but it's mostly that Microsoft demanded that 343 half-ass the story and put all the focus on the multiplayer live service side of the game (and that sweet sweet microtransaction cash) and leave the story campaign to wither with a bare bones story and no DLC to pad it out (despite original intentions for DLC by 343 once they got told to get the multiplayer stuff out ASAP and had to cut story content for time).<br /> <br /> Halo Infinite is a lot closer to V5 than W5: an attempt to keep the continuity with the previous games, while 'resetting' to something closer to the original formula (&quot;Master Chief and a ragtag group of survivors land on a mysterious artificial ring-world after losing a major space battle, and have to fight to survive, control the ring, and uncover the dangerous secrets it hides&quot; applies to Halo CE and Halo Infinite rather purposefully). You don't have to question if any of the plot of the previous games happened or not (they did), even if you have a lot of questions about what the hell happened during the time skip (a lot of which didn't get answered in the game). Unlike Halo fans though, TTRPG fans are used to reading supplements for more answers; most Halo fans don't want to have to read six tie-in novels to find out lots of details that probably should have at least gotten a bit of exposition in the games at some point (and 343's whole run has been bad about this in all three of their Halo games, not just Infinite). The state of the Halo plot in 2024 is actually in a pretty decent place, if you've read all the books, comics, and so on instead of just played the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T16:01:34-07:00","id":1532968,"title":"","content":"So my takeaway from this is that Halo 360 is kind of like Evil Dead 2...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T21:22:48-07:00","id":1532979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532934#post1532934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, is this direction they're heading into really worse than &quot;If you're a fan of the previous editions, this isn't for you.&quot;...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all but the amount of venom thrown at every single trace of Legacy lore by a certain contingent of W5 fans means that reintroducing it is going to cause ( is already causing) friction.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T23:11:59-07:00","id":1532983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532979#post1532979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all but the amount of venom thrown at every single trace of Legacy lore by a certain contingent of W5 fans means that reintroducing it is going to cause ( is already causing) friction.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A few days of reading through in-depth spirit descriptions and places to visit in the Umbra and a good lot of them will probably rethink a few things in favor of &quot;legacy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T23:13:00-07:00","id":1532984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532979#post1532979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all but the amount of venom thrown at every single trace of Legacy lore by a certain contingent of W5 fans means that reintroducing it is going to cause ( is already causing) friction.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And I ponder if this truly is the right direction due to that. W5 already has its playerbase who like it, those who like Legacy stick to Legacy. Trying to make W5 into legacy is just by mechanics really not worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T01:44:43-07:00","id":1532989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532984#post1532984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I ponder if this truly is the right direction due to that. W5 already has its playerbase who like it, those who like Legacy stick to Legacy. Trying to make W5 into legacy is just by mechanics really not worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the original sin here is that if W5 had truly wanted to live up to the &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-moniker, it should've gotten a stronger premise that is sufficiently distinct enough to stand on its own and can't be confused with the previous editions of WtA. But without that and the prospect of Renegade having to write one supplement per year... what else are you going to fill this setting with? Like with Tribes... Some of the names were changed and some concepts were broadened (like with Black Furies) but you're not exactly working there with a huge bounty of new original ideas either. When it comes time to write more about the Silent Striders, the old lore is still just sitting right there and it would be <i>very easy</i> to reintroduce that stuff back into W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T02:20:08-07:00","id":1532990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532989#post1532989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the original sin here is that if W5 had truly wanted to live up to the &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-moniker, it should've gotten a stronger premise that is sufficiently distinct enough to stand on its own and can't be confused with the previous editions of WtA. But without that and the prospect of Renegade having to write one supplement per year... what else are you going to fill this setting with? Like with Tribes... Some of the names were changed and some concepts were broadened (like with Black Furies) but you're not exactly working there with a huge bounty of new original ideas either. When it comes time to write more about the Silent Striders, the old lore is still just sitting right there and it would be <i>very easy</i> to reintroduce that stuff back into W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the original sin was that they scrapped the BNS version and then tried to do something new. Only for that not to work and I am guessing JA deciding it was a reimagening instead. Which meant a lot of the structure supporting the lore that came from the mechanics was removed and not replaced with anything.<br /> <br /> And here's the thing; If they had cut their losses with WtA and considered WHAT sort of werewolf game they WANTED to have in WoD5, I think they could have done better by doing an entirely new game. One that could have answered the want for a more typical werewolf game, something which W5 ironically has the perfect mechanics for.<br /> <br /> I know I keep harping about this, but there are people who don't touch WtA because they want a game focused on werewolves and not saving the world. W5 has potential to be that game.<br /> <br /> So if Shattered Nation forces the old lore back, it isn't really good for anyone. W5 has AWFUL mechanics to try and tell the legacy story, and if you liked W5's way of werewolves you'd not find the old lore fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T03:06:43-07:00","id":1532992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532990#post1532990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if Shattered Nation forces the old lore back, it isn't really good for anyone. W5 has AWFUL mechanics to try and tell the legacy story, and if you liked W5's way of werewolves you'd not find the old lore fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the W5 supplements could do what the V5 supplements did and ignore the mechanics or there's the nuclear option of explicitly decanonizing the W5 corebook as a Pentex Psi-op like the black hand book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T07:11:16-07:00","id":1533004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532992#post1532992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the W5 supplements could do what the V5 supplements did and ignore the mechanics or there's the nuclear option of explicitly decanonizing the W5 corebook as a Pentex Psi-op like the black hand book...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a Pentex psy-op... it's a BSD psy-op!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-23T02:17:26-07:00","id":1533034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1532990#post1532990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, the original sin was that they scrapped the BNS version and then tried to do something new. Only for that not to work and I am guessing JA deciding it was a reimagening instead. Which meant a lot of the structure supporting the lore that came from the mechanics was removed and not replaced with anything.<br /> <br /> And here's the thing; If they had cut their losses with WtA and considered WHAT sort of werewolf game they WANTED to have in WoD5, I think they could have done better by doing an entirely new game. One that could have answered the want for a more typical werewolf game, something which W5 ironically has the perfect mechanics for.<br /> <br /> I know I keep harping about this, but there are people who don't touch WtA because they want a game focused on werewolves and not saving the world. W5 has potential to be that game.<br /> <br /> So if Shattered Nation forces the old lore back, it isn't really good for anyone. W5 has AWFUL mechanics to try and tell the legacy story, and if you liked W5's way of werewolves you'd not find the old lore fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's particularly peculiar about that process going from the BNS-version to the Hunters Entertainment version to the WOD in-house team version isn't just about how the vision of what W5 is kept shifting. Rather what's even weirder about this is that it all got less specific and less substantive as well. With BNS the fall of the Garou Nation was a civil war with two factional blocs who had specific ideas of what it takes to turn things around. Fast forward to the version in the actual W5 corebook and the Garou Nation still fell... but now it just sorta happened * shrug * . Incredibly somehow the WtA Revised corebook with its 303 pages feels way more substantive and complete compared to the 334 pages of the W5 corebook as well. Same as with H5 having 288 pages and the original HtR corebook having 300 pages.<br /> <br /> Hard to imagine Paradox would've accepted &quot;cutting their losses&quot;, though, because originally W5 was supposed to be the follow-up to V5 and then after the switch to the in-house WOD-team at Paradox they announced that they needed more time and so in the meantime they released the H5 corebook. So they were already on borrowed time with this W5 release to begin with. In my opinion, this didn't end up going well for either release. Both have the feeling of being rushed to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-23T04:21:34-07:00","id":1533036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533034#post1533034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard to imagine Paradox would've accepted &quot;cutting their losses&quot;, though, because originally W5 was supposed to be the follow-up to V5 and then after the switch to the in-house WOD-team at Paradox they announced that they needed more time and so in the meantime they released the H5 corebook. So they were already on borrowed time with this W5 release to begin with. In my opinion, this didn't end up going well for either release. Both have the feeling of being rushed to some degree.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So in that context where dose that leave Shattered nation? Is that supplement Paradox's attempt they try to crowbar W5 back into a V5 follow up mancaics be dammed or another half measure...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-23T10:00:38-07:00","id":1533039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533036#post1533036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in that context where dose that leave Shattered nation? Is that supplement Paradox's attempt they try to crowbar W5 back into a V5 follow up mancaics be dammed or another half measure...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to see a trend in just one book, but how much formerly out material gets written back in with SN will probably be how the future goes, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-23T12:11:08-07:00","id":1533044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533036#post1533036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in that context where dose that leave Shattered nation? Is that supplement Paradox's attempt they try to crowbar W5 back into a V5 follow up mancaics be dammed or another half measure...</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it leave it...? Well, it leaves it where it is: A supplement Renegade is about to release. As for the rest, well, that's where it gets ambiguous. Depends on who you ask, I guess. And WOD5E has shifted directions so many times at this point in terms of who's doing what and what WOD5E is supposed to be like... Worst case, we're here a couple of years from now and the new lead-developer proudly proclaims that he had the bright idea that what WOD5E really needs is to stand on its own and detach all connections to previous editions (but it also can't go as far as CofD, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T05:21:59-07:00","id":1533074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533044#post1533044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worst case, we're here a couple of years from now and the new lead-developer proudly proclaims that he had the bright idea that what WOD5E really needs is to stand on its own and detach all connections to previous editions (but it also can't go as far as CofD, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they could go for the opposite extreme and try to integrate all lines into a single world regardless if the many canon conflicts it will cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T13:44:10-07:00","id":1533086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533074#post1533074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or they could go for the opposite extreme and try to integrate all lines into a single world regardless if the many canon conflicts it will cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can always go back and edit past releases, I guess. It's what Renegade did with the books from Onyx Path and Modiphius after all. And they didn't do a press-release or every showed any transparency for the changes they made.<br /> <br /> So in that mold, why wouldn't Renegade just do re-launches of the three corebooks while they include a multitude of rewrites which makes them more like WOD5.5E?<br /> <br /> But really, all of that's just pure speculation. As I've mentioned before in other threads, the real hinge-point for this project will be the release of Bloodlines 2. A lot is riding on that release. I mean, if it fails it would be easy to see a corporation like Paradox reach the self-serving conclusion that actually they had done nothing wrong and the real issue was that the WOD-IP had never been popular, to begin with. Just declare the WOD-IP to be a dumpster-fire and sell it to whoever for peanuts to save face (although, let's be honest, it would be a bit of a &quot;victory&quot; to sell something you declare to be shit to somebody).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T18:09:13-07:00","id":1533100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533086#post1533086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just declare the WOD-IP to be a dumpster-fire and sell it to whoever for peanuts to save face (although, let's be honest, it would be a bit of a &quot;victory&quot; to sell something you declare to be shit to somebody).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I would be carious If Paradox sold the IP to Games Workshop. They got a stable of competent writers with the black library so it would be quite fascinating to see what they would do when they have access to the WOD IP.<br /> <br /> Like I would pay a pretty penny to see a SI book written by Dan Abnett and I think a WTA book by Matt Ward would be plenty &quot;entertaining&quot; for some one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T19:26:41-07:00","id":1533103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533100#post1533100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I would be carious If Paradox sold the IP to Games Workshop. They got a stable of competent writers with the black library so it would be quite fascinating to see what they would do when they have access to the WOD IP.<br /> <br /> Like I would pay a pretty penny to see a SI book written by Dan Abnett and I think a WTA book by Matt Ward would be plenty &quot;entertaining&quot; for some one...</div> </div> </div> </div>My first choice in that scenario would be Aaron Dembeski-Bowden. Back in the day, when the WW forums displayed only one post per page and Apocalypse (along with the other ToJ books) was still far off on the horizon, he was a part of the W:tA community on the boards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T01:01:32-07:00","id":1533109,"title":"","content":"Given what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar479_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"479\" data-vbnamecard=\"479\">Damian May</a> has reported of the way W5 is played (weredogs,bhrhrr), I can totally see there being quite a bit of pushback from those liking W5 as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T07:09:51-07:00","id":1533123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533103#post1533103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My first choice in that scenario would be Aaron Dembeski-Bowden. Back in the day, when the WW forums displayed only one post per page and Apocalypse (along with the other ToJ books) was still far off on the horizon, he was a part of the W:tA community on the boards.</div> </div> </div> </div>ADB is good people. Though most of his writing was for WtF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T14:21:10-07:00","id":1533137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533123#post1533123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ADB is good people. Though most of his writing was for WtF.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only because the Apocalypse came before a number of people could get a gig freelancing for W:tA work. As I recall, Stu Wilson was in about the same boat, but he eventually saw some time as developer of W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T21:30:55-07:00","id":1533154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533123#post1533123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533137#post1533137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah despite what some people would say about WH 40K books there's plenty of gems among the catalog of the black library and plenty of authors that I think can do justice to the many aspect of WOD.<br /> <br /> Like Dan Abnett would be perfect for any hunter adjacent work, ABD while I personally think is not exactly the right guy for WTA, I could actually see him writing some pretty decent material for demon the fallen, I could see the guy who wrote the excellent Infinite and the Divine (or Trazyn's excellent adventure) could write a great mummy book exploring an Amenti's life as they live though thounds of years of history. I even can see Sandy Michell of Caiaphas Cain fame writing a book about Beckett that's pure pulp goodness.<br /> <br /> And if by some cosmic screwup Matt Ward writes a WTA corebook then well... It would be a 50/50 it would be solid update to existing lore or it would be a total 180 from W5 in the worst way possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T10:25:17-07:00","id":1533263,"title":"","content":"Honestly while I'd trust GW with WoD fiction I don't think much of their current ability to write lore for a game. It's probably me being a child of 4th and really disliking how modern 40k is cutting short it's actual epic storylines to focus on demigods (RIP Yarrick, you were supposed to die as Armageddon burnt). You also would run the significant risk of a crackdown on fanworks, possibly even the multitude of CofD fanlines.<br /> <br /> Although I'd also love to throw Rick Priestley at the setting, Beyond the Gates of Antares is just as good as Rogue Trader was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T03:48:07-07:00","id":1533449,"title":"","content":"Games Workshop has long since divested itself of making rpgs, though. They license that stuff ever since they ditched Black Industries. And I think they are better for focusing their stuff. I don't see them being interested in a urban fantasy ip as it would dillute their brand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T13:50:53-07:00","id":1533459,"title":"","content":"Hell, I'd love to write some WOD novels and know plenty of other professional authors who did write them and would love to do so again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T14:36:04-07:00","id":1533460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533449#post1533449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I don't see them being interested in a urban fantasy ip as it would dillute their brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like GW could just release any WOD under the white wolf label if they're so afraid of diluting they brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 04-01-2024, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T10:41:22-07:00","id":1533757,"title":"","content":"Ok...if I see yet another W5 Black Fury PC concept posted online that is ' fights against misandry' I'm gonna punch someone.....turning my two favourite tribes into a) off brand Spirals (RTs) and b) fucking Incel defenders ( BFs) annoys the crap out of me.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T11:41:18-07:00","id":1533758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533757#post1533757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok...if I see yet another W5 Black Fury PC concept posted online that is ' fights against misandry' I'm gonna punch someone.....turning my two favourite tribes into a) off brand Spirals (RTs) and b) fucking Incel defenders ( BFs) annoys the crap out of me.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Furies are now in the same boat as Brujah. You can say that people with strong convictions, political or otherwise, make good candidates for Embrace in the case of Clan Brujah. And then somebody takes that and starts talking about Nazi Brujah. Of course, in the case of the Black Furies, there's a particular angle that gives it an ironic edge to exploit the new broader framework to explicitly create W5 Black Furies that are against feminism. Although, even while giving this new version of the Black Furies this very vague focus on injustice in general, you could've tempered that by outlining various norms of Garou-society that would've created guidelines and prevented stuff like that. But the worldbuilding is lackluster in the W5-corebook, so yeah, that paved the way for misogynistic Black Furies, of course.<br /> <br /> With Red Talons, I'm really just baffled why it was written like that... Hunter-orgs, Sabbat, Fenrir... those were all too much badwrongfun and so had to be rendered unplayable as far as the official game is concerned. But having PCs who intentionally spread plagues is acceptable somehow...? No idea what possessed the writers to present the Red Talons like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T12:44:08-07:00","id":1533760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533758#post1533758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black Furies are now in the same boat as Brujah. You can say that people with strong convictions, political or otherwise, make good candidates for Embrace in the case of Clan Brujah. And then somebody takes that and starts talking about Nazi Brujah. Of course, in the case of the Black Furies, there's a particular angle that gives it an ironic edge to exploit the new broader framework to explicitly create W5 Black Furies that are against feminism. Although, even while giving this new version of the Black Furies this very vague focus on injustice in general, you could've tempered that by outlining various norms of Garou-society that would've created guidelines and prevented stuff like that. But the worldbuilding is lackluster in the W5-corebook, so yeah, that paved the way for misogynistic Black Furies, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fifth Edition World of Darkness was a mistake.&quot; - Hayao Miyazaki<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With Red Talons, I'm really just baffled why it was written like that... Hunter-orgs, Sabbat, Fenrir... those were all too much badwrongfun and so had to be rendered unplayable as far as the official game is concerned. But having PCs who intentionally spread plagues is acceptable somehow...? No idea what possessed the writers to present the Red Talons like that. </div> </div> </div>A perhaps more vital question - If the Red Talons are now the Ratkin, what are the Ratkin going to be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T12:59:48-07:00","id":1533762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally