character trans and clearfiy that misandry only applies to TERFS...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T16:36:08-07:00","id":1533773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533757#post1533757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok...if I see yet another W5 Black Fury PC concept posted online that is ' fights against misandry' I'm gonna punch someone.....turning my two favourite tribes into a) off brand Spirals (RTs) and b) fucking Incel defenders ( BFs) annoys the crap out of me.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm going to get off topic a little and risk adding fuel to the fire because of this, but I think there would be a possibility of this happening in the legacy, I mean, my reference is the revised version, but it is mentioned there that even if the furies are protectors of the defenseless they are also mothers, sisters, daughters and lovers, so I don't think it's impossible have someone that way. Anyway, what else can you say about this PC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T19:26:00-07:00","id":1533784,"title":"","content":"OK, so, in legacy if you wanted a &quot;good&quot; anti-misandry style character, you'd get something like a proponent of restorative justice that seeks to fight toxic masculinity and fix the damage modern society has done to men because that's an effective way to decrease the threats to the most vulnerable in society.<br /> <br /> &quot;We need to fight to protect incels&quot; would not work in legacy, but can fit in W5's presentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T20:39:05-07:00","id":1533795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533762#post1533762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean if they were normal Ratkin that would be kinda ok but they seem to be taking up Freak Aspect niches....which is fun.........wait.........CoF are Badly Coded Twitchers aren't they......</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I hadn't even considered that, but yeah, that's almost exactly what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T01:43:28-07:00","id":1533799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533784#post1533784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so, in legacy if you wanted a &quot;good&quot; anti-misandry style character, you'd get something like a proponent of restorative justice that seeks to fight toxic masculinity and fix the damage modern society has done to men because that's an effective way to decrease the threats to the most vulnerable in society.<br /> <br /> &quot;We need to fight to protect incels&quot; would not work in legacy, but can fit in W5's presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll have to explain this one better, why would this work on W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T05:16:28-07:00","id":1533808,"title":"","content":"1) W5 eliminated the larger Garou Nation and with it the Tribal cultures that enforced not allowing stretching the broad strokes ideals of the Tribes to be considered acceptable.<br /> <br /> 2) W5 removed the Furies focus on protecting those unable to defend themselves to attacking those seen as oppressors. <br /> <br /> So, without the social controls and cultural norms of the legacy Tribes, W5 Black Furies are free to pick whatever causes they personally believe in. So as there are real world people that believe there is an underclass of men that are being oppressed from flourishing by feminism and women enforcing a society where those men cannot thrive, there's nothing in W5 that would stop a Black Fury from taking up the same position and then fighting for &quot;justice&quot; by trying to demolish (verb!) feminist guided egalitarian society to liberate (verb!) the unfortunate men that weren't born with the ability to be Chads.<br /> <br /> I'm going to apply some brain bleach now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T05:28:40-07:00","id":1533809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533808#post1533808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) W5 eliminated the larger Garou Nation and with it the Tribal cultures that enforced not allowing stretching the broad strokes ideals of the Tribes to be considered acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Shattered nation then promptly reintroduce to some extent. Since one of the book's focuses is the Sliver Fangs and the garou king.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T08:15:43-07:00","id":1533817,"title":"","content":"We even have direct commentary from Justin Achilli about this very thing:<br /> <br /> (From the Discord Q&amp;A)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Are the black furies going to be changed into a more activist type tribe that stands against all kinds of oppression rather than their more gender focused theme in previous versions?</b><br /> <br /> Black Furies are broadly opposed to injustice (and therefore oppression), not any specific expression of it. So you could easily have a feminist Black Fury just like you could have Black Fury war protestor or a Black Fury against the carceral state or a Black Fury who wants to kill that one diner owner for groping his serving staff.<br /> <br /> <b>Do the black fury's accept anyone who thinks they are fighting injustice? Does this lead to infighting within the black furies due to opposing viewpoints who each think the other one stands for injustice?</b><br /> <br /> It's not up to the tribes to &quot;accept&quot; individuals, as you propose above. Tribe is all of the Garou pledged to a particular Patron Spirit, so as long as you make the pact with Gorgon, you're a Black Fury. Which is no guarantee that you'll be all buddy-buddy with other Black Furies, of course. </div> </div> </div>So it's very much the intention that when it comes to the focus on injustice in general, it's all very subjective and in the eye of the beholder what particular flavor of injustice the W5 Black Fury character is interested in.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Tribe Favor and Ban make it clear that the focus is more on opposing people in power and whatever flavor of injustice the PC cares about rather than defending the stuff the Tribe used to be interested in previously. The Favor is about opposing or circumventing someone or something in a position of power (relative to themselves or someone in their care). And the Ban is about Black Furies being expected to always correct perceived injustices.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T09:23:31-07:00","id":1533821,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;It's not up to the tribes to &quot;accept&quot; individuals, as you propose above. Tribe is all of the Garou pledged to a particular Patron Spirit, so as long as you make the pact with Gorgon, you're a Black Fury. Which is no guarantee that you'll be all buddy-buddy with other Black Furies, of course.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> I truly missed this part in all the other BS. This is quite unlike how even WtF first edition did it, as you still had to have contact with the tribe in order to join it.<br /> <br /> This treats the tribe basically like a vampire clan, where you can be embraced and be very ill-fitting. Seen also with the complete lack of ronin, which to this day baffles me.<br /> <br /> One has to wonder how joining a tribe actually works in W5, if a random monk can join Ghost Council and still be a monk....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:23:46-07:00","id":1533833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533821#post1533821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This treats the tribe basically like a vampire clan, where you can be embraced and be very ill-fitting. Seen also with the complete lack of ronin, which to this day baffles me.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair Garou who are a terrible fit for their Tribe but remain with it have always been something I've been interested in, but that was because of the (relative) lack of choice. Your Tribe is your family, and families have their black sheep and weirdos.<br /> <br /> The way W5 does it? It feels set up to encourage conflict between Garou due to differences, rather than cooperation in spite of them.<br /> <br /> Can somebody show actually has the book answer: does W5 present Garou on Garou conflict as more likely than fighting the Wyrm? Because I get the feeling that it's what somebody with sway over the game wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:32:48-07:00","id":1533836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533821#post1533821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&quot;It's not up to the tribes to &quot;accept&quot; individuals, as you propose above. Tribe is all of the Garou pledged to a particular Patron Spirit, so as long as you make the pact with Gorgon, you're a Black Fury. Which is no guarantee that you'll be all buddy-buddy with other Black Furies, of course.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> I truly missed this part in all the other BS. This is quite unlike how even WtF first edition did it, as you still had to have contact with the tribe in order to join it.<br /> <br /> This treats the tribe basically like a vampire clan, where you can be embraced and be very ill-fitting. Seen also with the complete lack of ronin, which to this day baffles me.<br /> <br /> One has to wonder how joining a tribe actually works in W5, if a random monk can join Ghost Council and still be a monk....</div> </div> </div> </div> My understanding is that Fifth Edition Garou explicitly choose their tribe - after being approached by one or <br /> more Patron Spirits, who will likely compete for the fairly small number of Garou making their first change in a year, in a series of dreams and visions - so Tribe, unlike Clan, is very much optional.<br /> <br /> If this is the case, then it seems logical that those chosen by a Patron Spirit will share elements of personality &amp; fields of interest that make them generally (Though not uniformly) compatible with their tribemates.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:37:06-07:00","id":1533837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533833#post1533833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair Garou who are a terrible fit for their Tribe but remain with it have always been something I've been interested in, but that was because of the (relative) lack of choice. Your Tribe is your family, and families have their black sheep and weirdos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually if a garou doesn't fit a tribe, they won't succeed in their RoP. Or another totem arrives to claim them. So ill-fitting garou generally don't happen. Garou born are an exception because they might fit in the tribe, but not be treated like it.<br /> <br /> W5, as far as I know, does encourage rejecting one's elders. But playable tribe vs playable tribe isn't that covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:40:00-07:00","id":1533838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533836#post1533836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My understanding is that Fifth Edition Garou explicitly choose their tribe - after being approached by one or<br /> more Patron Spirits, who will likely compete for the fairly small number of Garou making their first change in a year, in a series of dreams and visions - so Tribe, unlike Clan, is very much optional.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't really accurate, tribeless garou aren't mentioned in the book, even though you'd think some WOULD decline the spirit. All garou are stated to be part of some tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:41:36-07:00","id":1533839,"title":"","content":"Well, we have the book and I think the W5 corebook's take aligns with a pessimistic outlook on how much unity and harmony exists between Garou in general. So for Tribes, I think the relevant passage is from pg 40: &quot;Tribe membership confers some degree of culture and belonging, but all tribes consist of werewolves, who are passionate creatures and prone to infighting. Tribes are not lockstep perspectives, but fractious and factional groups based upon certain commonalities.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T13:24:27-07:00","id":1533846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533838#post1533838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't really accurate, tribeless garou aren't mentioned in the book, even though you'd think some WOULD decline the spirit. All garou are stated to be part of some tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given how darned dangerous the World of Darkness is for even while tribes of Garou, it\u2019s likely that Lone Wolves don\u2019t last very long\u2026<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T13:26:21-07:00","id":1533847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533846#post1533846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given how darned dangerous the World of Darkness is for even while tribes of Garou, it\u2019s likely that Lone Wolves don\u2019t last very long\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the example characters are essentially lone wolves with tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T13:40:47-07:00","id":1533849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533847#post1533847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of the example characters are essentially lone wolves with tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn\u2019t that an oxymoron? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T13:45:36-07:00","id":1533851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533847#post1533847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of the example characters are essentially lone wolves with tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>By contrast all the pregens from the first official adventure are explicitly normal tribal members who Oddly enough, don't really have any problems with the garou nation, indeed they actually expected support the local elder.<br /> <br /> Said elders are as I said in the thread about the adventure acted too passive about the situation but otherwise portrayed as totally helpful to the party and will join them in freeing the cearn in the climax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 04-08-2024, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T14:54:12-07:00","id":1533854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533809#post1533809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which Shattered nation then promptly reintroduce to some extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not enough to change any of what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T15:07:42-07:00","id":1533856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533854#post1533854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not enough to change any of what I said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not but it's quite telling that Renegade is welling to go agenst the intended tone the corebook set out in the first place is intresting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T16:05:56-07:00","id":1533858,"title":"","content":"Right now it's just messy. In a few years, when more books are out, and there's more clarity about the corebook vs. what Renegade is going to do with it, we can have a real discussion about how telling these things were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T18:34:20-07:00","id":1533865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533858#post1533858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now it's just messy. In a few years, when more books are out, and there's more clarity about the corebook vs. what Renegade is going to do with it, we can have a real discussion about how telling these things were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but the first major supplement and a official adventure (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review\">which has a thread on the forum</a>) basically went against the intended tone of the corebook.<br /> <br /> The adventure (Reclamation) especially since all the pregens for it are written as proper members of they tribes instead of lone wolves the corebook expects you to play. With at least one of them (the sliver fang) actually has links to the garou nation (in the form of him explicitly following in the steps of a garou hero). Also all the &quot;elder&quot; characters are portrayed as decent people doing they best to help Gaia (beside some issues with the timeline of the adventure) and at the end of the adventure the caern was reclaimed and is heavily implied it's to become a regional hub for garou activity and the pregens are assumed to carry out the legacy of the garou hero that used to watch over it. And the next suggested adventure actually involves artifacts recovered from the caern...<br /> <br /> Again this is the complete opposite of what the corebook intend tone as one one the posters in the aforenoted thread said it best:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533461-w5-adventure-reclamation-review?p=1533567#post1533567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as this is amusing, I have to admit it is also basically making W5 more like the Legacy. When a lot of people who got to W5 got to it BECAUSE they disliked the Legacy.<br /> <br /> It also means that the setting stated in the core is very much not present beyond it.<br /> <br /> That and also, this means that the people wanting to get into W5 after Shattered Nation releases are going to have a core that is USELESS in terms of garou culture. Not to mention returning to the issue where you need to know a lot more than the core to play WtA well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It almost as if the people from regrade realized that intended tone from corebook as written doesn't lend it self well to writing supplements or engaging adventures... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 04-08-2024, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T23:53:36-07:00","id":1533876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533849#post1533849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn\u2019t that an oxymoron?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so, but when the book has one example character be the head of a goddamn country, another a monk in an isolated monastery, one spreading disease and so on, how are you integrating them to your game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T00:25:02-07:00","id":1533878,"title":"","content":"Also, if the idea is that Tribes are now these fractious communities/culture that are barely recognizable as a coherent group and prone to infighting, then you'd have to seriously reevaluate some events in the setting. A Tribe acting as one would be hard to imagine like when the White Howlers all went into the Labyrinth and turned into the Black Spiral Dancers. And the description of the Cult of Fenris emerging (&quot;The Cult of Fenris is itself but a single facet of a greater tribe pledged to Wolf, but the Cult raised its collective voices louder, and those pledged to Wolf either joined them or found membership among the other tribes.&quot;) wouldn't make sense either. Having various factions with wildly different opinions within a Tribe should be the norm for all Tribes then, not this event that broke up the Tribe as described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T01:23:32-07:00","id":1533879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531801-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-shattered-nation-announced?p=1533878#post1533878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if the idea is that Having various factions with wildly different opinions within a Tribe should be the norm for all Tribes then, not this event that broke up the Tribe as described.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well evidently Renegade agrees with you since Reclamation features peregens who are portrayed as more normal tribal members who don't really have any problems with conept of the garou nation ( the sliver Fang is explicitly follower of one of the nation's past heros).<br /> <br /> And Shattered Nation is going to have to go into detail on the structure of sliver Fang by necessity since it features proment characters from that Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if the idea is that Tribes are now these fractious communities/culture that are barely recognizable as a coherent group and prone to infighting, </div> </div> </div>Yet by contrast one of the major beat of a Reclamation is two packs putting aside they differences and reclaiming a caern. Turing into a sanctuary for garou in the reagon.<br /> <br /> Talk about mixed messages eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}